{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon","id":922283,"title":"How do you modify your Classic World of Darkness from canon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T16:36:45-07:00","id":922283,"title":"How do you modify your Classic World of Darkness from canon?","content":"Exactly what it says in the title, describe how your campaign world differs from the one in any of the editions and how. I think all of us veteran gamers like to modify our world in ways big and small. I'd be interested in how you all present things and what changes you make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:43:18-07:00","id":922287,"title":"","content":"My V20 campaign is a combination of all the Editions.<br /> <br /> 1. The<b> Assamites</b> are still cursed by the <b>Tremere</b> and unable to drink blood. They also are capable of killing for hire but it's not all they do. The Vizier and Mage Bloodlines don't exist but they serve as functions within the clan which isn't just about the murder for hire.<br /> <br /> 2. The major WOD powers are all vaguely aware of each other. The Kindred, for example, believe the Illuminati (<b>Technocracy</b>) exist and call them that. They have a formal treaty which keeps them out of each other's hair and protecting the Masquerade/Consensus. It was negotiated by the Tremere who are still laughing at the Heremetics from beyond death.<br /> <br /> 3. The <b>Ravnos </b>had an ancient powerful member of their clan awaken who slaughtered a large number of Indian Ravnos as well as humans but there was no Week of Nightmares. There's a fierce debate over whether it was an Antedeluvian or not.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Tzimisce </b>are exactly like the Old Clan Tzimisce but possess Vicissitude. They're more cold scientists and transhumanists than freaks for the sake of freakydom.<br /> <br /> 5.<b> Independent clans</b> are welcome to live in the Camarilla cities as long as they swear to abide by the Traditions. Hence, Assamites, FoS, Giovanni, and Ravnos are all possible to be found as citizens of cities.<br /> <br /> 6.<b> The Sabbat is basically a failed experiment </b>as the founders were meant to be heroic wariror poets and philosophers but 90% of their thinkers as well as teachings go over its sects members heads. A small group of Sabbat are posthuman geniuses and Nieztschean supermen but they are disgusted with their own sect. The last Great Sabbat War caused the sect to collapse into smaller philosophical movements which are considered extinct (but aren't).<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The True Hand a</b>nd <b>Inconnu </b>are two branches of the same organization. Basically, Kindred older than God manipulating the younger vampires against each other.<br /> <br /> 8.<b> No Thaumaturgy Paths </b>exist but the Path of Blood and Necromancy with both requiring separate discipline points. Rituals are more powerful, though.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Mummies</b> exist but the 1E ones and a handful of ones they've made since Set.<br /> <br /> 9. The <b>Cappadochians </b>still exist but in service to the Giovanni as a small number were allowed to survive in exchange for swearing allegiance. The Samedi are a result of a withering like condition which sometimes strikes them. No Harbinger of Skulls ever existed.<br /> <br /> 10. The<b> Salubri </b>are still surviving but there's less than a hundred in the world and of all the variations of the original clanbook. The Tremere generally try to have them killed but make a half-hearted gesture about it at best. Most masquerade as Ventrue or Toreador with some weaker ones as Caitiff. They did not join the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 11. <b>Sabbat Paths of Enlightenment </b>are slightly less demanding of EVIL with the Path of Harmony considered akin to vegans in the sect but not worthy of destruction. Some Camarilla Elders still follow the Old Ones or have created their own.<br /> <br /> 12. <b>Anarch Free States </b>don't exist anymore since they eventually faded to become identical to normal Kindred cities. Chicago's population was forced out by the Sabbat and migrated to New York City. Many Kindred are reluctant to return to the fallen cities even if the Sabbat have been driven out. Thus, New York is grossly overpopulated with 500 Kindred.<br /> <br /> 13. <b>Kuei-Jin Exist but are less racist: </b>Kuei-Jin are basically just Asian Risen/Mummies and while more organized than their fellows are about the same level of numbered and far less numerous than regular vampires. Asiastic versions of the 12 Clans inhabit the Far East alongside the Kuei-Jin. I've canonized the Gentleman Gamer's Eastern Kindred.<br /> <br /> 14. <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> wholesale replaces <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b>. Elements remain, though, with the Civil War between the Pure Ones and Forsaken having started in the 1990s and pretty much sealing the death kneel of the Garou race.<br /> <br /> 15. <b>Pentex </b>has since been taken over by the Camarilla and is now an enviironmentally friendly corporation devoted to preserving mankind as food for the next few thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-27-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T08:32:00-07:00","id":922648,"title":"","content":"With MtAs, the Avatar Storm happened but things have dissipated, the Traditions and Technocracy are largely in a state of uneasy cold war and the Disparate Alliance is coming together, not all the Crafts have joined yet but they are gaining steam. Oh and it's less about the fight against the Nephandi and more about survival and standing up to the Trad/Tech dominance in the Mage world.<br /> <br /> For VtM, Week of Nightmares hasn't happened yet, the Gangrel haven't left the Camarilla and the Anarch Movement has become the Third Sect. The Kuei-Jin are vampires but they are not exclusive to Asia, the majority of them rise there. The Courts of the West Coast of North America have become an independent network of courts that is more modern and pragmatic in their outlook. They've made an uneasy peace with the local Anarchs and Camarilla in an attempt to cover up that no longer have the support and resources they had when they first invaded. At the same time, Hong Kong is a struggling Camarilla bastion in China, being aided under the table but other Kuei-Jin Courts that hate the Quincux, the Kindred of India and the Giovanni. Though the latter is also helping the Chinese Kuei-Jin, playing both sides against the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:45:32-07:00","id":922689,"title":"","content":"I mix-match between old and new a lot with hints of homebrew all over the place.<br /> For VtM, the Requiem Convenants (sects) are existing alongside the classic ones. The Camarilla basically started as a large attempt to bring entire Clans together in united purpose; didn't quite go that way but hey, they're the biggest Sect today so something went right. The Cappadocians and Salubri still exist, though they're nolonger considered Clans; most hide with the Invictus cuz the Tremere can't touch them there lest they risk a Sect war which neither the Camarilla nor Invictus wants. Also there are a lot of Assamites hooking up with various Sects (most notably the Camarilla, Sabbat and Lancea Sanctum) what with the schism and all.<br /> <br /> Ashirra are a sub-Sect of the Lancea Sanctum, Baali were basically Dark-Ages Belial's Brood (who now carries the infernalist torch).<br /> Tremere Antitribu are dangerously low in number, but not eradicated. Gangrel are essentially one step from becoming the &quot;Clan of the Circle of the Crone&quot; since they left the Camarilla, some of the few eastern Ravnos are pondering options after the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement is an evolvement of the Anarch Movement which aims to get more structure and &quot;rebuild the system&quot; which most of the hardcore Anarchs are not a fan of, cuz they think that having a system in the first place will lead to corruption eventually; so there are some conflicts there.<br /> Ordo Dracul is same old, but have some homebrew Coils and VII is an honored group of essentially kamikaze warriors of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Camarilla covers most of western Europe and the east coast-midwestern US. Sabbat Mexico, Spain, notable parts of South America, parts of Canada, and are fighting for control around the US. Carthian Movement hangs around the West Coast, Anarchs exist wherever more or less. Ordo Dracul are mostly in Romania and Oceania in terms of actual strongholds, but otherwise are found in lots of places since they pursue various knowledges world-wide. Circle of the Crone are the strongest around Africa, India and parts of the more rural US and Canada. Lancea Sanctum are mostly in the mediterranan and the Invictus mostly hang around eastern Europe and Russia with some encroachment into Asia.<br /> <br /> I also mix Generations and Blood Potency. All Vampires start with Blood Potency 1, but each dot in Generation places a hardcap on how far down it can fall in torpor and so on. So for example, a 10th Generation will still have to work his way up to Blood Potency 4; but once he has it he cannot drop below 4 under any normal circumstances, not even by torpor. If he goes above his Generation limit however, it can drop down to 4 again. This way Blood Potency allows for character progression with a bit of risk while still maintaining Generations and making having a low Generation (and Diablerie) highly desired.<br /> Also Kiasyd are Embraced Changelings a l\u00e1 Dark Ages V20; thus their origin and Sect is a lot more up in the air. They all gain Mytherceria, but the other two Disciplines are chosen from the parent Clan. A Lasombra-Embraced Kiasyd for example could have Mytherceria, Obtenebration or Dominate, or he could pick Potence instead of Obtenebration or Dominate.<br /> Also Kuei-Jin are Sin-Eaters a l\u00e1 Geist (see below) and Samedi, Gargoyles and Blood Brothers are the only Bloodlines that exist, the rest never happened; especially not the Daughters of Cacophony.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf I also mix-match old and new and got both &quot;Gaians&quot; and Forsaken running around doing their thing. Black Spiral Dancers are hated by everyone much like Bale Hounds and even the Pure can agree to momentary truces to hunt them down first. I also tend to play Spirits in a tad more one-dimensional human way than the corebook suggests which I imagine a lot of people would flog me for. Fera also exist btw; cWoD style.<br /> <br /> For Mages, same old. Mix factions etc. Pentacle Orders, Traditions, Technocracy, Fringe Factions and Seers of the Throne are the main ones. Banishers remain a thing but they're less &quot;came back wrong&quot; and more often former hunters or people who can't handle the pressure or so and lash out violently. Marauders are scary and nobody knows where they come from or how they do what they do; they're more akin to &quot;came back wrong;&quot; but I leave it to mystery on just what is wrong with them. Tremere Liches are renamed Styrian Liches to differ from the Vampire Clan and I use a homebrew Arcana of Abyss which belongs to a sixth Path called Scelesti awakening to the Watchtower of the Empty Road; there are still heavy persecution of them and discussions on what to do in the Awakened communities.<br /> <br /> Hunters are mostly Vigil with small Reckoning elements like Bystanders being a thing and some factions. Slashers are not supernatural (unless they take up one of the other templates).<br /> <br /> Demon is full Fallen, albeit heavily homebrewed to fit with the nWoD system. They're very close to Spirits, but different beings ultimately. They're wrong about God creating everything, rather he stumbled upon it and made some attempts at playing Sims with the world before the whole rebellion left a sour taste in his mouth and so he left. The Loyalists I'm still not sure if I want them around but distant or gone as well. There are some adjustments to Factions too. Pentients wanna get back in God's good graces, Reconcilers focus on humanity instead and wanna get cuddly with them again since the whole rebellion was about them and all (or was it). Renegades are unaligned and Faustians are more objectively cold and exploitive of humanity generally speaking.<br /> <br /> Infernal Demons (from WoD: Inferno) exist, but are a lot more Spirit-based and likely originating from Pandemonium. They differ in origin and splat from the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Geist is about 99% in effect, I rarely draw from Wraith but I have one or two really obscure elements here or there from Oblivion. All in all though, Geist is the deal. Few fan-made Keys around, and as said the Kuei-Jin are Sin-Eaters who are just about the only faction of Sin-Eaters with organization and &quot;governmental&quot; structure; for once putting an organization in Asia rather than the US or EU, which is also why the Vampires haven't been able to settle in any large scale in Asia without making heavy concessions to the Cathayans. Otherwise it's about the same as the core game.<br /> <br /> Changeling is full Lost.<br /> Prometheans exist.<br /> Mummy is full Curse.<br /> Princess the Hopeful and Genius the Transgression are in play; for the most part so is Siren though I'm largely holding it off until it's done other than occasional sightings.<br /> <br /> That's about all I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:42:18-07:00","id":922721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7060_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7060\" data-vbnamecard=\"7060\">Karavolos</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Carthian Movement is an evolvement of the Anarch Movement which aims to get more structure and &quot;rebuild the system&quot; which most of the hardcore Anarchs are not a fan of, cuz they think that having a system in the first place will lead to corruption eventually; so there are some conflicts there. </div> </div> </div>Love your combining ideas! I think the idea of the Carthian Movement as the modern day expression of intelligent Anarchs like Critias. Menele, and Ecaterina the Wise. It also has a good place of making people like Maldavis a contrast against people like Juggler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ordo Dracul is same old, but have some homebrew Coils and VII is an honored group of essentially kamikaze warriors of the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>For me, the Ordo Dracul is a secret subsect of the Tzimisce and Tremere (!) who decided they were less interested in dominating the world than just doing science so they invited the most intelligent and cold-blooded vampires of the world to join them in the name of science as well as understanding the Kindred condition.<br /> <br /> Quite a few High Blooded Cainites are a member which would get the order in serious trouble if either sect found out (it's hard to say if it would get them eradicated because, well, they're pretty damn powerful and secretive). I'd make it the group people seek out if they want to learn Thaumaturgy regardless of clan or sect affiliation. You just have to find them.<br /> <br /> VII I'd just say is the True Black Hand, killing the worst of vampires (or the inconveinant) to keep the world safe from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Werewolf I also mix-match old and new and got both &quot;Gaians&quot; and Forsaken running around doing their thing. Black Spiral Dancers are hated by everyone much like Bale Hounds and even the Pure can agree to momentary truces to hunt them down first. I also tend to play Spirits in a tad more one-dimensional human way than the corebook suggests which I imagine a lot of people would flog me for. Fera also exist btw; cWoD style. </div> </div> </div>In my campaign, the werewolves found out Father Wolf was wyrm corrupted and the Garou divided into the factions of those who blamed it on (or for) the War on Rage, the Impergium, werewolves being racist, genocidal nutjobs vs. those who felt it was them not going far enough. The Forsaken (Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Wendigo, Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Stargazers, and Uktena) found themselves at war with the Pure (Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Red Talons, Get of Fenris, and weirdly the Fianna).<br /> <br /> Because that's what reality needed right now. A genocidal war between those two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters are mostly Vigil with small Reckoning elements like Bystanders being a thing and some factions. Slashers are not supernatural (unless they take up one of the other templates). </div> </div> </div>Slashers are the nickname in my campaign for Imbued who have gone cra-cra and are full on Waywards--worse, that a lot of Imbued switch to become them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon is full Fallen, albeit heavily homebrewed to fit with the nWoD system. They're very close to Spirits, but different beings ultimately. They're wrong about God creating everything, rather he stumbled upon it and made some attempts at playing Sims with the world before the whole rebellion left a sour taste in his mouth and so he left. The Loyalists I'm still not sure if I want them around but distant or gone as well. There are some adjustments to Factions too. Pentients wanna get back in God's good graces, Reconcilers focus on humanity instead and wanna get cuddly with them again since the whole rebellion was about them and all (or was it). Renegades are unaligned and Faustians are more objectively cold and exploitive of humanity generally speaking. </div> </div> </div>My version of Demon is that humanity is infectious. Being bonded with humans has allowed some to redeem themselves in ways which no one ever expected (demonic possession should, after all, be permanently the demon in control) but SOMETHING changed. Also, Demons speaking in Judeo-Christian terms is a combination of using their hosts language (the ones in the Far East use Buddhist or Shinto terms) as well as the fact their memories are muddled by the merging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:20:20-07:00","id":922744,"title":"","content":"I dont make any major changes, I do however de emphasize some things, with a focus on &quot;Decamping&quot; Cwod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:38:47-07:00","id":922823,"title":"","content":"Each campaign I run tends to be a little different here and there based on what kind of stories I'm going for, but in general these are the 'options' I go with.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire the Masquerade</b><ul><li>About 2/3 of the Gangrel leave the Camarilla, they retain a Justicar and full 'clan' status though due to a number of important Gangrel elders that chose to remain in the Camarilla.</li> <li>Ur Shulgi wakes up and breaks the blood curse of the Tremere and begins purging 'disloyal' elements of the clan. Because of the purge the schismatic Assamites seek to join the Camarilla and are accepted in response to the Gangrel leaving and the appearance of more bloodlines among the Sabbat (Harbingers of Skulls and Salubri <i>antitribu </i>for example).</li> <li>The Salubri Warrior and Healer castes still exist in the Middle East, protected and hidden by the Ashirra's influence.</li> <li>[Ravnos] did not wake up, the week of nightmares did not occur and the Ravnos are still an independent clan.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Mage the Ascension </b><ul><li>The Avatar Storm never occurs.</li> <li>Doissetep is not destroyed.</li> <li>The Technocracy is not controlled by the Nephandi or other forces, however individual divisions may have fallen (Special Projects Division has been suborned by Pentex and the Wyrm for example).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T01:06:35-07:00","id":923130,"title":"","content":"This is for vampire only because I think it's the splat which doesn't fit for crossover rules or the lore of the other splats. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are lupines, they once had their special gifts but now only a few off them have them, their time is over, if no wonder occurs.<br /> <br /> Mages are Powerful sorcerer, they have a mana rating, which allows them to do their fancy magic but if it's empty they have to use the normal sorcerer rules.<br /> <br /> Rest of the splats stay more less like they are now.<br /> <br /> The week of nightmares will be slightly different in my chronic. It will not be the Ravnos Anti that goes crazy. I have yet to decide. <br /> <br /> There are different origin stories and neither has been universally excepted. <br /> <br /> Sabbat is less cartoonishly evil and more a power house to be feared, do too their more military-like organisation.<br /> <br /> No true black hand for now, maybe this changes after I read the new book but old ones was terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:59:57-07:00","id":923253,"title":"","content":"Canon? I destroy it totally, because I would rather to create a mash-up mixing different tittles, like Ravenloft and some ideas from Kult: lost divinity.<br /> <br /> This isn't our real world but a cursed demiplane, and some darklords rule cities with &quot;arcologies&quot; (super-skycrapper buildings). <br /> <br /> The masquerade was totally broken in the past, but now there aren't vampires, at least people believe no in their regions. <br /> <br /> Som vampires created &quot;ganado&quot;, a special parasite to infect creatures, a demi-undead or necrotouched like the ones from &quot;Resident Evil 4&quot; to collect blood/vitae. <br /> <br /> The Garou Triad (Weaver, Kaos and Wyrd) are powerful like megacorporations or emperors, but not true deities. Wyrd doesn't want to taint all, but &quot;improve all with biopunk technology&quot;. Weaver doesn't want &quot;frozen order&quot; and Kaos doesn't want to destroy all order, but they want &quot;dinamic order&quot;.<br /> <br /> They fays aren't worried about children don't believe Toothfairy and Tinkerbell effects. <br /> <br /> Metropolis is a &quot;poken universe&quot; where the vampires don't need keep the Mascarade...(but the fay lords can give them some annoying surprises).<br /> <br /> Prometheans or half-golems can be created by other supernatural creatures, even by vampires.<br /> <br /> Fays are the children by titats, who lost ancient war againts &quot;archons&quot; (deities). The lictors (from Kult rpg) and fays hate each other. <br /> <br /> Some vampires can use &quot;biopunk cauldrons&quot; to collect blood by animal. <br /> <br /> Some vampires with &quot;weak blood&quot; (14th generation) can be daywalkers with a special &quot;biopunk suit&quot; but they are totally blinded by sunlight.<br /> <br /> Some vampires can be &quot;healed&quot; but really become &quot;reborn&quot; of mummies, after a long time in the afterlife realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:37:50-07:00","id":923770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love your combining ideas!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Ordo Dracul is a secret subsect of the Tzimisce and Tremere (!) who decided they were less interested in dominating the world than just doing science so they invited the most intelligent and cold-blooded vampires of the world to join them in the name of science as well as understanding the Kindred condition.<br /> <br /> Quite a few High Blooded Cainites are a member which would get the order in serious trouble if either sect found out (it's hard to say if it would get them eradicated because, well, they're pretty damn powerful and secretive). I'd make it the group people seek out if they want to learn Thaumaturgy regardless of clan or sect affiliation. You just have to find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I play them as a full-fledged Sect, albeit a small one, with origins from the Tzimisce (being founded by Vlad Dracul and all), but we have the same idea that it's about the only place left where Tremere and Tzimisce stand a chance of working together (not counting the rare Antitribu in the Sabbat) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The Ordo definitely value knowledge and the sharing of information, including Disciplines, but to me I imagine that while 'Discipline trading' is not uncommon, lots of Vampires are greedy or don't wanna share snowflake traits, so it isn't exactly a walk in the park to learn unique stuff either; with the notable exception being Coils of the Dragon which the Ordo developed specifically to trade amongst its members. Otherwise we have nearly the same idea I feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VII I'd just say is the True Black Hand, killing the worst of vampires (or the inconveinant) to keep the world safe from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I differ VII and the True Black Hand as the latter being the secretive elite assassins while the former are more kamikaze/suicide bombers. VII members are honored for their matyrdom and enjoy prestige to their name, especially if successful; but also lead very dangerously by going into enemy territory and essentially fucking shit up. Breaching the Masquerade here, causing epidemics there, targeting neonates and other young blood, manipulating people into enmity with each other, even Infernalism if it helps. Whatever it takes to hurt the enemies of the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> The True Black Hand stay more in the shadows and carefully take out enemies with more precision and subtlety than the VII and sometimes act as the enforcers of the Sabbat by making sure members play by the Sabbat's rules, the few there are. If some Bishop is a traitor, the TBH is sent against him. If some Pack are causing a war with the Giovanni and give the finger to anyone trying to stop them, the TBH is called. If the Camarilla is being held together in a place by a competent Prince and little else, TBH goes in for the kill. If a city is assaulted by Lupines and the Sabbat is having trouble fighting them, the TBH will start identifying key-targets and so on.<br /> TBH is a bit of an open secret in the way that few talk about them, but the information is out there for those who look. In some cases, successful VII-ers who do well with subtlety stand a decent chance to get recruited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my campaign, the werewolves found out Father Wolf was wyrm corrupted and the Garou divided into the factions of those who blamed it on (or for) the War on Rage, the Impergium, werewolves being racist, genocidal nutjobs vs. those who felt it was them not going far enough. The Forsaken (Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Wendigo, Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Stargazers, and Uktena) found themselves at war with the Pure (Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Red Talons, Get of Fenris, and weirdly the Fianna).<br /> <br /> Because that's what reality needed right now. A genocidal war between those two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep the (Wt)Forsaken Tribes and simply mix them with the WtA ones myself. I like the idea of some believing Father Wolf got corrupted by the Wyrm though! I think I'm gonna use that in the future. Out of curiosity, what do you do to the Silent Striders?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slashers are the nickname in my campaign for Imbued who have gone cra-cra and are full on Waywards--worse, that a lot of Imbued switch to become them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I play Hunters as regular people with little (or much) more knowledge than most that might or might not be equipped for the job. Aka Vigil <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Sufficed to say, Slashers to me are no more imbued than anyone else is, at best they might have some supernatural splat or another, but all in all &quot;slashers&quot; is just a name for &quot;serial killer.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=922721#post922721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My version of Demon is that humanity is infectious. Being bonded with humans has allowed some to redeem themselves in ways which no one ever expected (demonic possession should, after all, be permanently the demon in control) but SOMETHING changed. Also, Demons speaking in Judeo-Christian terms is a combination of using their hosts language (the ones in the Far East use Buddhist or Shinto terms) as well as the fact their memories are muddled by the merging.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run the Demons with about full knowledge of who they are and whatnot (unless they have an Amnesia Flaw or so) who, when they take over the host, take on traits that the host's brain has, explaining knowledges, memories and habits. Some Fallen are more susceptible to this than others, the highly Tormented in particular tend to resist a host's influence, and some might need more time to get their minds out of the gutter than others but otherwise they generally know they are (Fallen) Angels. I never really bought the idea that being stuck in a black room with some screaming will automatically torment you beyond redemption; so the Fallen are not automatically at Torment 10 until they possess someone in my games. Though I think it's a personality thing for me. Headaches aside, doing nothing at all does not bother me generally due to my slothful nature.<br /> <br /> Being the nWoD system you might not be interested, but I also play Torment like the Supernatural Advantage with the drawback being that if you go too far, you start becoming more demonic and unable to rely on Low-Torment Lores. A Fallen can overcome it all the way to Torment 0 (with exp and a bit of effort that might or might not succeed) and if they manage they nolonger need hosts to stay out of the Abyss (unless they gain Torment again through evil deeds or by using any High-Torment ability); though without a host it becomes difficult to interact with things outside of Twilight without breaking the Masquerade.<br /> Being without Torment, they'll lose out their Supernatural Advantage since they're essentially embracing their nature as beings created to serve (as opposed to High-Torment Fallen who rebel against their nature and everything else around them) and any usage of High-Torment abilities will put them back at Permanent Torment 1, even if it normally would've caused Temporary Torment (and from there it goes on normally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:30:52-07:00","id":924135,"title":"","content":"If I was to do a V:tM campaign, I would take a little from Woodward and make the Brujah a Sabbat clan and keep the Cappadocians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:01:39-07:00","id":924153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924135#post924135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was to do a V:tM campaign, I would take a little from Woodward and make the Brujah a Sabbat clan and keep the Cappadocians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Camarilla would be boring as all get out!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:15:58-07:00","id":924207,"title":"","content":"I'm going to copout and say I don't have &quot;one&quot; world of Darkness. It honestly depends on the game in question. If I want to play up Vampire: The guilded Cage. I emphasize how much other monsters hate you and how easy Hunters find you. There are only a few safe spots.. and those are taken by more powerful elders. If I want run league of extraodinary Vampires doing archaeological stuff.. well its much safer to travel.<br /> <br /> Well lets see I'll go with one of my more fun variants which had afew character types including a Fallen, a KOTE, a Mage and a Kitsune. God, The Jade Emperor, the Demon Emperor, Gaia.. these are Titles. Titles for beings of incredible power but Titles that have in fact been handed off over time.<br /> <br /> The previous God had stepped down as was to be the case at the end of the 5th age and went on to do whatever Ex Gods do. The angels tried to cheat the system and almost succeeded.<br /> <br /> Here's what an angel looks like: <a href=\"http://safebooru.org/index.php?page=post&amp;s=view&amp;id=1777783\" target=\"_blank\">http://safebooru.org/index.php?page=post&amp;s=view&amp;id=1119559</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Unfortunately they sort of got stuck in not understanding they won so they kept playing the system until a proper Demon Empress Emerged: <a href=\"http://safebooru.org/index.php?page=post&amp;s=view&amp;id=1777783\" target=\"_blank\">http://safebooru.org/index.php?page=...iew&amp;id=1777783</a><br /> <br /> So being a bunch of Highly selfless individuals who totally don't think they could run the universe better things went. &quot;Well&quot; That is to say at least the horror of the universe could ulitiamtely be said to be the players' Fault!<br /> <br /> This would not be the first or last time I've used an anime as background canon..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:31:57-07:00","id":924213,"title":"","content":"A couple of thoughts I had which apply to the broader World of Darkness I have:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Technocracy and Traditions are at peace</b>: Well, more like a Cold War but the Avatar Storm provides so much more interesting fodder with both sides having been decapitated and fully intending to get around to murdering each other but it's been 17 years since then and that means there's a slight majority of people now (albeit low-level ones) who have never been at war with the Union as well as see the Traditionalist-Union conflict stupid. Even more so, all the leaders who HATE each other were fighters in the 90s so even the Traditionalists love technology while the Technocrats are kind of wondering why the hell anyone gives a crap about mages versus the literal VAMPIRES nearby.<br /> (Which kind of hurts the peace treaty between them and the Camarilla)<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Gangrel never left</b>: I don't see why they would anyway because there's no chance they're really going to get any better offer alone than they are with the Camarilla, whether they take it seriously or not.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Imbued are a finite number</b>: Imbued still exist in this game but actually take the place of True Faith for the most part. There's a bunch of Hunters blessed by what they believe to be God's grace which give them a variety of oddball powers against monsters. They can be psychopaths or serial killers or saints but they are real and there's always about a 1000 of them in the world. Other Hunters are uncomfortable with them but it makes them a little harder to deal with. Sullivan Dane is one in my games and he's immortal.<br /> Literally. He comes back from the dead when you kill him.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>&quot;Cyclical Nephandi&quot; replace regular Nephandi</b>: I mentioned this in the mage forum but Nephandi are less a bunch of Always Chaotic Evil psychos than a bunch of insane Gnostics who want to destroy reality so they can transcend and become God(s) with a capital G of their own perfected universe. They believe casting this reality down to oblivion is the only way to do it as it's hopelessly broken and flawed with Paradox.<br /> <br /> This argument ACTUALLY MAKES SENSE to mages (albeit is hugely extreme) and that's the terrifying part. The Cauls are ostensibly showing the true nature of reality which warps a soul to this goal forever.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Gehenna is Cyclical</b>: The Methusaleh's Thirst is a curse of Caine on vampires so all vampires eventually develop it and must eat their own children to gain their full power on awakening. However, the nature of torpor and vampires are no one really remembers the original Second City. A truly ancient vampire like Menele, Helene, or Ur-Shulgi may well be Third Generation as far as anyone knows it.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Hazimel was destroyed during the Week of Nightmares</b>: Because I like the idea a 4th generation vampire was that terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2019, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:09:09-07:00","id":924219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924213#post924213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. <b>Imbued are a finite number</b>: Imbued still exist in this game but actually take the place of True Faith for the most part. There's a bunch of Hunters blessed by what they believe to be God's grace which give them a variety of oddball powers against monsters. They can be psychopaths or serial killers or saints but they are real and there's always about a 1000 of them in the world. Other Hunters are uncomfortable with them but it makes them a little harder to deal with. Sullivan Dane is one in my games and he's immortal.<br /> Literally. He comes back from the dead when you kill him.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me I drop True Faith as anything but a Numina. I'm more than willing to have powers that require having Faith and you know being a Vampire but they work like other Vampire powers. I like to explore other aspects of Faith than just &quot;it can produce magic powers or its not real&quot; that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:23:13-07:00","id":924230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924219#post924219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me I drop True Faith as anything but a Numina. I'm more than willing to have powers that require having Faith and you know being a Vampire but they work like other Vampire powers. I like to explore other aspects of Faith than just &quot;it can produce magic powers or its not real&quot; that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the disturbing revelation that people can believe in God and repulse you with their belief but this is a good compromise.<br /> <br /> Buy True Faith like any other Numina.<br /> <br /> Rating x7","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:33:31-07:00","id":924237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924230#post924230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't mind the disturbing revelation that people can believe in God and repulse you with their belief but this is a good compromise.<br /> <br /> Buy True Faith like any other Numina.<br /> <br /> Rating x7</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not bothered by the fact that people can believe strongly in God that they can set people on fire with it. Its more the implication that when a person sets on on fire with gasoline because they believe really strongly in God that their Faith is some how not as &quot;Real&quot;. That it is in fact any more intrinsically a sign of the Divine than any other mechanic. That being a really Faithful person can't lead to really bad places like a short trip to wassail because all your Faith is in Hate and malice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:11:46-07:00","id":924581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924207#post924207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, The Jade Emperor, the Demon Emperor, Gaia.. these are Titles. Titles for beings of incredible power but Titles that have in fact been handed off over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>HMM, something to consider for my own games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924207#post924207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previous God had stepped down as was to be the case at the end of the 5th age and went on to do whatever Ex Gods do. The angels tried to cheat the system and almost succeeded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume &quot;Angels&quot; mean Loyalists rather than the Fallen, and if so how did they try to cheat the system? As I mentioned elsewhere I need to figure out what to do with the Loyalists in my game, I figured I might rip-off someone else's work here 8D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924207#post924207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would not be the first or last time I've used an anime as background canon..</div> </div> </div> </div>No shame there as long as you and your players are having fun. And if it helps, I use anime backgrounds all the time; you're not alone on that front. For the Greater Weeaboo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:55:09-07:00","id":924599,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm considering is making dhampyr a non-Thinblood thing. Vampire men can, uh, make their equipment work and that actually allows the production of seed and the siring of children. It also makes the women ghouls for the duration of the pregnancy (which defies the usual rules of such). If the child is born, they effectively have all the functionality of a Revenant from birth which can lead to a lot of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:39:51-07:00","id":924646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924599#post924599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm considering is making dhampyr a non-Thinblood thing. Vampire men can, uh, make their equipment work and that actually allows the production of seed and the siring of children. It also makes the women ghouls for the duration of the pregnancy (which defies the usual rules of such). If the child is born, they effectively have all the functionality of a Revenant from birth which can lead to a lot of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a fifth level necromancy power that allows a vamp to be &quot;Human&quot; for a day. I can imagine one vamp going a little crazy being able to experience life again and slipping up. After all dhampyr myths have existed for a while...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:41:30-07:00","id":924648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=924581#post924581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume &quot;Angels&quot; mean Loyalists rather than the Fallen, and if so how did they try to cheat the system? As I mentioned elsewhere I need to figure out what to do with the Loyalists in my game, I figured I might rip-off someone else's work here 8D</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how accurately you can say they are Loyalists since they've been around for multiple turnovers. The system is sort of set but the prophecy of Ages is also sort of set. They tried to cheat the system by raising up a non Demon Emperor for the Sixth Age Godhead. And it worked.. for abit. Unfortunately they didn't quite know it worked so they kept tinkering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No shame there as long as you and your players are having fun. And if it helps, I use anime backgrounds all the time; you're not alone on that front. For the Greater Weeaboo! </div> </div> </div>I should come entirely clean here. This particular game basically used the Puella Magi Madoka Magica series as &quot;canon&quot; for the universe. Some of the Not so Fallen angels became Incubators, the goal was to make a New God who would be a right and proper moral God from young Girls who wanted a single wish, these were not the most human understanding of angels.<br /> <br /> But it worked! Madoka became God. But she didn't understand what they were doing and they didn't understand she had ascended to Godhood because she removed all memory of her except with Homura.<br /> <br /> And then Rebellion happened and the game began with Demon Empress Homura sitting on the Throne of Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:51:06-07:00","id":924676,"title":"","content":"This is another idea which I'm only experimenting about in my &quot;cyclical Gehenna&quot; idea:<br /> <br /> <b>The Blood God Ascension Theory of the WoD</b><br /> <br /> Vampires aren't actually a race which is ten thousand years old but actually closer to a million with countless primordial pre-human man which was hunted and stalked by said creatures. Whenever they would compete for territory, they would devour each other's blood. The thing about generation is, and very few know this, it actually &quot;stacks&quot; so a vampire who ate a dozen 13th generations would raise a generation if he was 12th to 11th.<br /> <br /> When you reach 3rd generation or so, you start becoming so powerful or dangerous that you can hunger for vampire blood exclusively and basically devour all of your childer to make the Ascension from 3rd to 1st generation when you promptly ascend to become a kind of supernatural godlike being. This can also be achieved with simple age or power as well, though most vampires do it that way.<br /> <br /> This actually means the current crop of 4th generation Methusaleh like Menele, Helena, Hazimel, and Ur-Shulgi are the &quot;Antedeluvians&quot; of this era with the 3rd generation of the past having already effectively ascended past the point of relevance. It also means that the other Elders are going to start devouring neonates thanks to irresitable biological urge in order to become the next crop of clan lords.<br /> <br /> When they devour the majority of childer in this generation, the 3rd generation will then sire their own new crop of offspring with their names as the Clan. They will rule for thousands of years until they, too, feel the need to transcend or are destroyed by their fellows. Indeed, some of the diablerie of the last Antedeluvians was simply because their bodies weren't in torpor so much as abandoned. This is why Saulot, Lasombra, and Tzimosce didn't give a crap about their deaths. Amusingly, this also means Lambach will be a Antedeluvian this cycle of gehenna and he's decidedly up for avenging himself on the clan that disrespected him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2019, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T03:17:15-07:00","id":926955,"title":"","content":"My personal World of Darkness borrows from both the Old and the New World of Darkness:<br /> <br /> - Vampire: The Masquerade exists as is, but the Gangrelare still part of the Camarilla.<br /> - Werewolf: The Apocalypse is pretty much 1:1. Pentex and its subsidiaries are the primary business rivals of the various Technocratic fronts.<br /> - Mage: The Ascension has Horizon still around (no Avatar Storm or anything). The Disparate Alliance is a thing, and there's no Technocratic civil war (yet). Reality Deviants are captures when possible, but are not actively hunted down.<br /> - Wraith I'm still working on to see how I like it best.<br /> - Changeling is going to be some kind of mix between Dreaming and Lost. The kithain exist, but there is also the Gentry who don't take kindly to their prizes escaping from their realms. Most of the kithain stay out of these conflicts though, but some cannot help but accidentally get involved,<br /> - Hunter: The Vigil has most of its Compacts and Conspiracies exist, but a few are a bit different:<br /> -- Aegis Kai Doru: Front for an Arisen cult.<br /> -- Cainite Heresy: Run by Caine.<br /> -- Cheiron Group: Run by... things. Tend to get into conflict with Pentex and the Progenitors.<br /> -- Division Six: A front run by a high-up Technocrat to hunt down Reality Deviants.<br /> -- Knights of Saint Adrian: Empowered by a Fallen (a Devil, but not an <i>Earthbound</i>) to hunt down other Fallen.<br /> -- Knights of Saint George: Actually a cult worshipping the most powerful demon still in the Abyss.<br /> -- Les Mysteres: Let themselves be possessed by Banes.<br /> -- Lucifuge: The descendants of the Nephilim.<br /> -- Promethean Brotherhood: Their rituals come from a Nephandi.<br /> -- Talbot Group: The spirits they encounter are frequently Banes.<br /> -- Task Force: VALKYRIE: The highest rungs are infiltrated by Ventrue.<br /> -- Utopia Now: Seek to deal with Earthbound and turn their powers to their purposes. (This goes as well as you think it would).<br /> -- The Imbued are their own Conspiracy. They have three Creeds, which determines which Edges you get to buy and use: Mercy, Vision and Zeal.<br /> -- Finally, Slashers are around as well. They are immune to Disquiet and can form Kinship with Beasts, while at the same time being unable to sate the Hunger of said Beasts.<br /> - Mummy is a mix of Resurrection and Curse: you are raised up at the instruction of the Judges but you mostly fight the forces of Apophis and collect artifacts to keep them out of the corruptor's hands.<br /> - Promethean exists as is.<br /> - Beast exists as is. Note that Beasts are immune to the Disquiet of the Prometheans, their Lairs are immune to the Wasteland and they will never be the target of their Torment.<br /> - Demon: The Fallen is how Demons roll. No God-Machine or anything like that: Fallen do their thing in this World of Darkness while trying to deal with the other things that go bump in the night. Lucifer's reveal in LA did not happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T20:51:11-07:00","id":927432,"title":"","content":"For Vampire.<br /> In Werewolf the forsaken terms, the ravnos are the belial hounds. They infiltrate citys and destroy them from the inside. (I took their morality path very very literal).<br /> The Baali are a faction of the followers of set. The followers of set have Ofuscate, presence and Daimoinon (as being able to see weakness is really useful to tempters), serpentis can be learned later. In western countries the Followers of Set function as the publically &quot;accepted&quot; face of the clan while the baali are the hidden one because &quot;making a deal with the devil is obviously bad, making a deal with guys from a Egyptian religion is totally not the same&quot; and this is inverse in countries in which the Catholicism is weaker.<br /> Ahrimanes arent a all female cat vampire people. They are a bloodline result of a gangrel embracing a kinfolk. Their form is more wolf than cat.<br /> <br /> For werewolf.<br /> Kalindo is not a supersecret martial art. I just take ingenuity and a firm knowledge of martial arts.<br /> No Star gazers.<br /> The Imminent strike camp of the CoG get a bonus to learn any other secret rite or combat style of their choosing (they must pick one).<br /> Samuel Heighs was a GW kin (this is inspired by the GW Rev tribebook and it issue with kinfolks)<br /> CyberWolves are a growing threat.<br /> Garous can forge Klaives.<br /> <br /> <br /> For mage.<br /> Nobody cares about the ascension war anymore. Everyone lost, the higher ups of both faction push for it and the lower members make some token efforts or true efforts when a mage of the other faction goes off the rails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-06-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T23:52:32-07:00","id":927470,"title":"","content":"Vampire: blood potency and factions of requiem except they are much more powerful and the clans are masquerade. While cain is the predominant origin story among elders and the lancea sanctum (who say cain was the first but that the curse was given to others by God, including Lilith who would be known as the crone and the vampiric version of Satan, and their founder) there is little to no evidence and many modern and non Abrahamic worshipping vampires scoff at the idea. Some vampiric elders have been speaking of the final nights. While this lead to many kindred believeing the end was nigh in the late eightees and early nineties by 2000 they where all sick of it being the &quot;final nights&quot; and by now most princes would blush if they could if asked about it. The weak of nightmares never happened as there are no elders that powerful even if myths of such elders abound. <br /> <br /> Werewolf: the changing breeds only think they are related to gia. If she exists in the way werewolfs see her that is only because they believe that (via mage consciousness). The wyld, wyrm, and weaver are immensely powerful entities but are not the creators of the universe, nore are they more powerful than other immense umbrood like Luna, Helios, or whoever is the spirit of all the worlds oceans. However the conflict between them does exist and they are using the changing breeds as puppets, this war that was was started by the wyld. You see the werewolves think she is losing; that as nature dies so does she, but she is wining this war. As it rages on the world gets more chaotic and as it gets more chaotic she gets stronger, who cares if some perfectly ordered ecosystem gets destroyed? It just makes the world less balanced which means it's more chaotic! To accomplish this she secretly made the weaver insane, had her bind the wyrm and make him insane, then pretended to be dragged into the upcoming war. She then manipulated the shapechangers into worshipping a false entity that just happened to be on her side, and the other two decided to use that to their advantage. Doing things like forging the black spiral dancers and manipulating the anasi who where very different from the other changing breeds. Now they all fight for a goddess that probly does not exist in a conflict that honestly isn't as world shattering as they think it is. And the only way to end it is to stop the wyld, or get the changing breeds to realize the conflict is mostly pointless. <br /> <br /> Mage: nearly six hundred years the traditions and technocrats fought. Then the avatar storm hit. They both made a peace treaty believing that in their weakened state they stood no chance against the other (technocrats lost most of their organization, and traditions lost most of their masters). This mixed with other issues caused by the storm such as a technocratic civil war, the threat null, infighting over the replacements for the horizon council, and the need for more masters, kept the two groups busy for around fourteen years until the avatar storm ceased and most of their problems resolved. But then at that point they are now reluctant to fight. The Technocracy has become much more lax and doesn't really care about magic as long as it's not hurting anyone (that includes spreading &quot;false&quot; information like alternative medicine through direct practice and denying science although they'll start with refuting the magick user and end with mysterious disappearance as a last resort) and most tradition members either never fought in a war with the Technocracy or fought only briefly before the storm hit, most of those with a full vendetta against them are dead as they died from the avatar storm, or they died trying to take on the Technocracy alone during the cease fire because of the rouge councils influence. Not only that but both of them acknowledge that they have other enemy's to deal with. The Technocracy has noticed the multiple world spanning conspiracys that threaten them, and spiritual threats that assault the masses on a regular basis. Tradition members mostly want to just get on with their lives and work together to deal with supernatural threats and deal with hunters. Both have noticed the increased nephendic activity and the large assortment of marauders that where created from the storm that nobody tried to deal with. While officially both parties are enemies it is not uncommon for individual members to interact in a friendly manner or for individual cities of council mages to work with the Technocracy (or for both parties to be in an all out war only within the city). Also the disparate alliance does not exist and neither the traditions nore the majority of crafts care about ancient fewds that no one was alive to be at. Those few crafts and individuals who still take offence to conflicts that are over five hundred years old are ridiculed and usually ignored... unless of course the person was there and is now an an arch mage or oracle (most where powerful enough to survive the storm) then you hope the near omnipotent mage knows how not to hold grudges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T00:35:15-07:00","id":927476,"title":"","content":"Currently running a <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> &quot;mega-chronicle&quot; (all the published scenarios, with some original stuff to form &quot;connective tissue&quot; between them, and tweaked to fit in Denver, Colorado), and really hammering the &quot;personal horror&quot; theme. Some of the things I've done:<br /> <br /> - Included the Fog of Ages thing from <i>Requiem </i>(which also helps explain the &quot;Caine myth&quot; and Noddist apocrypha)<br /> - Also included the Predator's Aura thing<br /> - Any and <i>all</i> blood expenditure counts towards the generational maximum (Want to spend blood to heal, but you've already spent it on Celerity this turn? Too bad, unless you're a low gen.)<br /> - Used my revamped (pun intended) combat rules to make damage more consistent and dangerous (which has lead my players to a) strike first, fast, and decisively; and b) don't get into a fight unless they know they can win)<br /> - Cyclical Gehenna (Fog of Ages again, and possibly canon depending on how one interprets certain source texts)<br /> - Willpower rolls are always done at the characters current (temporary) rating - permanent Willpower is more a &quot;the size of the gas tank&quot; kind of thing<br /> - Celerity works more like <i>Dark Ages</i>, where more dots negates multiple action penalties<br /> - Not really a modification, but different splats use equivalent (or close to) Disciplines and such, like how they're presented in the Antagonists chapter<br /> - Finally, if it's not in <i>V20</i> (with very few exceptions), it's not in my game (so things like Abyss Mysticism and Anarch Sorcery simply don't exist. Which isn't a problem, as I don't have players interested in those things)<br /> <br /> A couple of other, smaller things I'm sure I'm forgetting, but those are the big ones.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:12:04-07:00","id":927821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=927476#post927476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Finally, if it's not in <i>V20</i> (with very few exceptions), it's not in my game (so things like Abyss Mysticism and Anarch Sorcery simply don't exist. Which isn't a problem, as I don't have players interested in those things)</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, do you mean just in the V20 core rulebook? Thaumaturgy particular to the Anarchs gets detailed a lot more in the V20 <i>Rites of the Blood</i> supplement than anywhere I recall seeing in earlier editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T20:36:08-07:00","id":927930,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> I do. The only books I use are <i>V20</i> core and <i>Companion</i>, and the Revised era books: <i>Revised</i> core, <i>Storyteller's Handbook</i>, and <i>Guide to the Camarilla/Sabbat</i>. I let my players know that if something's not referenced in those books, I probably won't allow it in the game.<br /> <br /> I am interested in using the kraina system from <i>Rites of Blood</i> but none of my players (or the story) are really directed towards that interest.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 07-08-2016, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:51:55-07:00","id":929484,"title":"","content":"The Apocalypse (and Gehenna by extension) were prevented by a grand alliance of Garou, Fera, Kuei-jin and Kindred. The Antediluvian vampires were discovered, bound by the greatest of rites, trapped in tungsten coffins and sent to Venus. There are a few other changes as well (Humanity 8+ vampires can ignore daylight and sunlight), but they are minor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:07:11-07:00","id":929661,"title":"","content":"For my WtA LARP we work on an &quot;all sources from 1st to revised are real&quot; approach, working them out that all scenarios coexist.<ul><li>Albrecht has the crown, but he is a big deal mainly for the other septs in his direct vicinity. He is not a global leader. Neither are Gogol, the Margrave or any other NPC or Organisation.</li> <li>There are no global tribe governing bodies. Politics are made in septs, period. If they are bad, the neighbour septs will deal with it, most likely lead by the closest Silver Fang sept.</li> <li>Camps are not organised, for the most part. They are sub-culture like philosophies within the tribes. Some are multi-tribal, because it makes sense, others aren't because it wouldn't make sense, if the were.</li> <li>The Gleaming Eye/Austere Howl conflict isn't usually violent.</li> <li>There are no septs of predominantly regional tribes in parts of the world, where they have no right to be. No Uktena in Japan, or Russia, no Wendigo in Africa.</li> <li>Pure Breed and Past Live/Ancestors are tribe specific. If you don't life by the traditions of your tribe you loose Pure Breed.</li> <li>Septs are usually mono-tribal or bi-tribal. Only a minority of a 2nd tribe is usually allowed to settle within an given septs territory.</li> <li>Garou are born garou and can be identified as such. No &quot;one can't discern the difference&quot;, like in W20.</li> <li>Game mechanics don't apply to character backgrounds. The story needs take precedent.</li> <li>All other WoD games basically exist, due to the cheer power we use mages only rarely. Since we ignore the 6th maelstorm and it's events just as much as the TB Silent Strider revised, we usually don't go into Orpheus and it's background.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:58:08-07:00","id":929695,"title":"","content":"I have modified my WoD a lot and have talked about these modifications endlessly. But this is a thread dedicated to setting hacks, so here we go....<br /> <br /> 1. The Revised Metaplot never happened. Gangrel are still in the Camarilla, the Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation, the Ravnos are still a full clan, there was no Week of Nightmares and no Avatar Storm. By and large, the entirety of Revised is declared non-canon in my games.<br /> <br /> 2. There are no Kuei-Jin and no Fallen in my games. KOTE and Demon are declared non-canon, and East Asia's cities are dominated by Cainites.<br /> <br /> 3. The themes of my games reject personal horror and instead embrace a mix of action-horror and dark politics. Nothing wrong with personal horror but it's not for me, so instead I go for action-horror and political intrigue, which I vastly prefer instead. My games can best be summed up as &quot;Black Lagoon with Fangs&quot;.<br /> <br /> 4. The aesthetics and atmosphere of my WoD games are neither Gothic nor Punk. Instead, I prefer a more anime-inspired approach. Again, nothing wrong with Gothic-Punk, but it's not for me.<br /> <br /> 5. The fan-game Senshi: The Merchandising is at least somewhat canon in my WoD games. Sailor Moon is definitely part of my WoD head canon. It may sound silly, but I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:33:06-07:00","id":930030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=929695#post929695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sailor Moon is definitely part of my WoD head canon. It may sound silly, but I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you and your players are having fun, that's what matters the most however your particular boat might look and float.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T21:58:09-07:00","id":930171,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely do the virtue-vice system instead of the nature-demeanor. I always felt that fit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:48:33-07:00","id":930695,"title":"","content":"Kote does not exist and Asia has normal clans with an Asian flavour. <br /> <br /> New York was taken by the camarilla in the 80s and not later as it is in New York by night. <br /> <br /> The anarchs of California didn't last long and the cities there are contested. <br /> <br /> Baali make pacts with earthbound <br /> <br /> Demons began to appear because of a weakening in their prison because the sixth maelstrom has not happened. <br /> <br /> Wraiths continue to march towards oblivion <br /> <br /> The technocracy is not a thing. There are mages and the consensus is a thing but there are no alliances of any sort they simply argue back and forth about &quot;the way things really are&quot;<br /> <br /> Technology becoming the general consensus isn't because of any organisation it stems from subconscious memories from the time of Babel when the rebel Angels were trying to uplift mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T02:11:28-07:00","id":930748,"title":"","content":"Does anyone actually have the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla? It's such a terribad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-13-2016, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T03:25:29-07:00","id":930757,"title":"","content":"I modified the Humanity System of Vampire as such:<br /> <br /> My modifications are simpler:<br /> <br /> * A vampire does not need to make a Humanity roll if they kill in self-defense or the defense of an innocent person after Humanity 7. This doesn't mean they feel GOOD about it, quite the opposite, but it doesn't cause them axiomatically to become worse people. This prevents cops and soldiers from all becoming Humanity 5 psychopaths.<br /> <br /> * Vampires do not have to make Humanity rolls for killing for blood or gain after Humanity 4.<br /> <br /> * Humanity 1-3 vampires are only the most sickest murderous degenerates alive.<br /> <br /> * Frenzying and killing someone in Hunger causes Humanity loss until you're down to Humanity 4 and 3 if it kills children other innocents.<br /> <br /> * Executing someone doesn't lower your humanity past 6 if they're genuinely evil or a viable threat.<br /> <br /> * Most Camarilla Elders stabilize at Humanity 4 and 5 with the general attitude of &quot;Do not kill people for fun or in sick games but kill people to preserve the Masquerade or gain power.&quot; They have the same attitude as mobsters.<br /> <br /> * Most Camarilla Ancilla generally have Humanity 5 or 6 with Humanity 6 vampires being ones who try not to be bad people but are tough enough to survive Kindred's harsh society. Humanity 7 vampires exist but they tend to be outliers.<br /> <br /> * Humanity 7-8 &quot;friendly&quot; vampires are painfully moralizing and usually either separate themselves from Kindred society or fall off the wagon. These are the vampires struggling with their curse actively. They tend to be Neonates or Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> * Humanity 9-10 vampires generally are hermits among their kind or pacifists who do their best to subsist on animal blood and use their powers actively for good. They tend to be Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> * Suicide is not uncommon for Camarilla vampires embraced with high humanity after their first few (accidental-usually) kills. Those that survive tend to have strong wills to live or connections to others.<br /> <br /> * Most Sabbat vampires generally go all the way down to 2 and 3 Humanity where they behave as serial killers and psychopaths. They tend to live fast and die young unless they have Paths, which are really hard to do. Wassail is not uncommon but taken care of by the Packs. The Vinculum holds and prevents them from attacking their former packmates, which makes them easily dealt with. Quite a few are staked then unstaked in Camarilla territory as the &quot;leave the dog in the woods&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> * Humanity 0 requires an &quot;Act of Ultimate Darkness&quot; like diablerie, demonic pact, sadistic torture, or slaughtering a school bus full of children. Personal betrayals also work for this but generally its diablerie.<br /> <br /> * Diablerie is not only an automatic Humanity loss, it's an automatic PATH loss even on paths that extol it. This results in diablerie becoming something which is done only as a very important rite or as an intense sanity-blasting experience.<br /> <br /> With my modified Humanity rules, I might also steal something from Bloodlines but I admit I never implemented it.<br /> <br /> * Points of Humanity can be restored to a Kindred which go above and beyond their current humanity score to do something good at the cost of an advantage or personal sacrifice.<br /> <br /> A Kindred who rushes into a burning building to save a mortal, a Kindred who destroys an evil artifact despite its potential boons, a Kindred who helps a Salubri escape at the cost of his relationship with the Tremere, and so on can get a point back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-13-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:06:04-07:00","id":930814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930748#post930748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone actually have the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla? It's such a terribad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, it was one of the many reasons as to why I despise the Revised metaplot.<br /> <br /> Also, on an unrelated note, I like how you reworked Humanity. Normally I chuck Humanity out of my games entirely, but I might use your modified version of it in one of my games instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:24:07-07:00","id":930817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930814#post930814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, it was one of the many reasons as to why I despise the Revised metaplot.<br /> <br /> Also, on an unrelated note, I like how you reworked Humanity. Normally I chuck Humanity out of my games entirely, but I might use your modified version of it in one of my games instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I gutted the metaplot in my games.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, I did introduce the Withering and had it kill 1/3rd of the vampires in the world and used it as the basis as a backstory for my current chronicle. I ruled it mostly killed the Sabbat and the worst of Kindred society which allowed things to be marginally better for chronicles about Humanity vs. The beast since players were less focused on a war between two equally awful factions. Sabbat are terrorists now rather than actual sects.<br /> <br /> I also had it break up into five different subgroups:<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul: </b>Sabbat scientists who no longer care about the war with the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <b>Belial's Brood:</b> Sabbat on the Path of Evil Revaltions or those who just want to be EVIL.<br /> <br /> <b>The Loyalists: </b>The Sabbat in miniature. Basically Sabbat ISIL.<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Hand:</b> A military organization devoted to slaying the Antedeluvians and ancient Kindred.<br /> <br /> I'm considering having the Assamite Join the Camarilla plot happen, though, and the Sabbat reconstitute around the Assamite Antitribu but I like my current world. I also am having the Giovanni join the Sabbat,<br /> <br /> Ditto the Setites and the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:29:51-07:00","id":930821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930817#post930817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I gutted the metaplot in my games.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, I did introduce the Withering and had it kill 1/3rd of the vampires in the world and used it as the basis as a backstory for my current chronicle. I ruled it mostly killed the Sabbat and the worst of Kindred society which allowed things to be marginally better for chronicles about Humanity vs. The beast since players were less focused on a war between two equally awful factions. Sabbat are terrorists now rather than actual sects.<br /> <br /> I also had it break up into five different subgroups:<br /> <br /> <b>The Ordo Dracul: </b>Sabbat scientists who no longer care about the war with the camarilla.<br /> <br /> <b>Belial's Brood:</b> Sabbat on the Path of Evil Revaltions or those who just want to be EVIL.<br /> <br /> <b>The Loyalists: </b>The Sabbat in miniature. Basically Sabbat ISIL.<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Hand:</b> A military organization devoted to slaying the Antedeluvians and ancient Kindred.<br /> <br /> I'm considering having the Assamite Join the Camarilla plot happen, though, and the Sabbat reconstitute around the Assamite Antitribu but I like my current world. I also am having the Giovanni join the Sabbat,<br /> <br /> Ditto the Setites and the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. A bit of an overly drastic change for me and my games, but I could see it working.<br /> <br /> I hope you'll like my games, a love letter to the days of 1e and early 2e and a mix of heavy political intrigue with a little bit of action-horror on the side. I mention this because I am thinking of running a VTM play by post game right here on these forums. I will probably either set it in 1e's Chicago (only in 2016 instead of 1991) or make my own NPC's for a custom setting, haven't decided yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T06:32:31-07:00","id":930822,"title":"","content":"It's a change I don't intend to actually make long as I'm mostly about single city affairs but it's stuff happening in the background which may affect the PCs and will happen over years gametime, if ever.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure I will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T07:30:15-07:00","id":930835,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Paths of Enlightenment</b></span><br /> <br /> * All Paths of Enlightenment have two variations. There's the Humane and Monster roads. The Humane Roads have Self-Control rather than Instinct even as they still have Conviction. They also have modified Hierarchy of Sins which justify murder under specific circumstances but tend to avoid mass diablerie or cruelty.<br /> <br /> * Paths cannot be sensed by other Kindred with no one able to tell when or where someone is a Path follower or a Humanity follower.<br /> <br /> * Path followers of 10 tend to radiate majesty the way other vampires radiate humanity at 10. They do not put vampires or humans uncomfortable but have a mildly beguiling presence. This has no mechanical benefit other than they do not look corpse-like but simply exotic.<br /> <br /> * Paths of Enlightenment are things which require immense acts of faith and meditation to achieve. To start on them is to essentially convert to a new religion and mindset before spending each and every day focusing on them.<br /> <br /> * It takes two to four months of intense study to convert to a Path and you can exchange a point of Humanity for a point of Path for each success on an Intelligence + Occult role when it's done. When done, you lose any remaining Humanity points. The difficulty is determined by your role-playing.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat's understanding of Paths are actually incomplete with most understanding incapable of being achieved past 5 due to the Vinculum, Pack Politics, and Sabbat propaganda. To seek higher than Path 5 is to do your own research or have a mentor.<br /> <br /> * Members of the False Hand can achieve Path 10 as can True Hand members, Inconnu, Baali, Followers of Set, Assamites, Ravnos Elders, Old Clan Tzimisce, Nagaraja, and several Camarilla Gehenna cults (where Kindred spirituality survives).<br /> <br /> The late Cardinal Moncada was one of the few Sabbat experts on Kindred spirituality, not just the Path of Night, and his death has greatly weakened the Sabbat there.<br /> <br /> * It is suggested Path Followers can achieve Golconda while others believe they achieve something more akin to the Kuei-jin's Bodhivisata state. Given the nature of Golconda and whether it relates to God's forgiveness or not versus an Eastern state of becoming one with the Beast, it's anyone's guess which is true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T07:32:58-07:00","id":930836,"title":"","content":"Sorry for deluging on house rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T15:28:57-07:00","id":931044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930748#post930748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone actually have the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla? It's such a terribad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do follow the metaplot in that Clan Gangrel left- though a lot of them are still staying in the Sect -but the metaplot reason of &quot;because a justicar said so&quot; is at best icing on the cake. I haven't thought too deeply and mostly go by my nature as a canon defender, but from the top of my head I imagine the Clan- exceptions aside -were never truly huge on the Sect overall. They worked with them and did what they had to yes, but the Camarilla never really represented anything the Clan appreciated. The uppers look down on &quot;low clans,&quot; they don't let the Gangrel hunt or embrace as they will, the cities encroach on the wilds, Gangrel Princes are a fair rarity compared to Ventrue ones and so on so forth. That one of the more respected Gangrel in the Camarilla left because the uppers practically laughed him out over his (wrongful) suspicion of having encountered an Antediluvian at most swayed younger Gangrel and those who were looking for an excuse to leave anyway without being considered a potential threat or so.<br /> In conclusion, the Clan formally left, but there are still plenty of Gangrel around with Primogen in place that they are still very much a part of it; so the future holds one of two routes that I see:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gangrel do leave, but it's a slow and steady pace and takes years before the effects are really felt.<br /> 2. Eventually the &quot;Clan Gangrel&quot; members who left are just considered renegades to the main Clan; not enemies necessairly but more autarkis of sorts who don't want anything to do with the Camarilla. Fine, as long as they don't do anything stupid, but they don't speak for the Clan in practice (if even in theory) anymore than the Antitribu do and the ones that are really listened to are the Outlanders who sit with the rest of the people in the Camarilla, high or low in terms of position.<br /> <br /> I have yet to decide any particular route I care to take with it, mostly cuz Vampires tend to take long with anything they do (being biologically immortal and all) and mostly cuz I don't run any Vampire games in writing moment which makes Vampires a background factor more than anything; i.e. limited sight and comings and goings of their world in the PC's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930748#post930748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also am having the Giovanni join the Sabbat,</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the Giovanni join with what is described as &quot;Vampire ISIS&quot;? Feels a bit uncharacteristic for them to me.<br /> I like your reworking of Humanity too; for the sake of my own simplicity I think I will stick to the regular (if slightly modified) Humanity used in nWoD, but I could see potential to use the rework as a form of &quot;alternate humanity&quot; working akin to a Path of Enlightenment for those who come to terms with their being while still keeping a balance between man and beast. Always kinda bugged me how there was no middle ground; you're either one with the Beast or you're fighting it.<br /> One thing that I feel confused on, speaking of Paths, is this bit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=930748#post930748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Diablerie is not only an automatic Humanity loss, it's an automatic PATH loss even on paths that extol it. This results in diablerie becoming something which is done only as a very important rite or as an intense sanity-blasting experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this make sense for the Path of Blood which is more or less built around Diablerie? I think Path of Caine also have a tendant in there urging it. Do you have any exceptions to the rule or how do you compensate for &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don't&quot; scenarios that arise from the paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:00:37-07:00","id":931078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would the Giovanni join with what is described as &quot;Vampire ISIS&quot;? Feels a bit uncharacteristic for them to me. </div> </div> </div>Well, I hope my players aren't reading this as it's basically the big campaign twist of the game's current &quot;season.&quot; The Giovanni are apparently joining the Camarilla and ingratiating themselves with everyone but the Tremere are suspicious (surprise, surprise) and keep trying to say there's something wrong here. In my New York by Night game, they attempt plays on acquiring the stock market and other Ventrue holdings while the PCs gloat (not liking the Ventrue).<br /> <br /> Only during the DRAMATIC HEIGHTS OF THE GAME will it be revealed the Giovanni intend to hand New York over to the Sabbat. Augustus foresees signs of Gehenna and having awakened (which, by itself, should be a sign of Gehenna) is interested in having the Sword of Caine at his side to aid him in his plan to plunge the world into eternal darkness as a means of combating the Antedeluvians. IF the PCs disrupt the ritual at the height, Augustus will get sucked into the Underworld by Cappadocius' ghost and the Giovanni in New York will go insane before they escape and the Giovanni will be forced into the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni joining adds a +2 to the Sabbat's collective Intelligence Attribute and helps them reform from their current divided state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like your reworking of Humanity too; for the sake of my own simplicity I think I will stick to the regular (if slightly modified) Humanity used in nWoD, but I could see potential to use the rework as a form of &quot;alternate humanity&quot; working akin to a Path of Enlightenment for those who come to terms with their being while still keeping a balance between man and beast. Always kinda bugged me how there was no middle ground; you're either one with the Beast or you're fighting it.: </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm trying to work on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does this make sense for the Path of Blood which is more or less built around Diablerie? I think Path of Caine also have a tendant in there urging it. Do you have any exceptions to the rule or how do you compensate for &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don't&quot; scenarios that arise from the paradox? </div> </div> </div>It's not an attempt to judge diablerie on a moral level as there's worse things, IMHO. However, it's an attempt to establish on a fundamental level <u>diablerie fucks you up</u>. Merging your soul with the soul of another vampire who is permanently trapped in your blood until you die screws with your ability to combat the Beast if you believe in pacifist Jesus or Vampire Murder Satan.<br /> <br /> With Road/Path of Blood NPCs, it's not a big deal as diablerie screwing with them just means they have to spend a lot of time in prayer, contemplation, and meditation to get their head on straight. Which fits because they're a death cult. For PCs, it's mostly a warning they're going to have to pay for their actions in good roleplaying or EXP (more likely the former).<br /> <br /> Also, I'm a low combat game so multiple diablerie is almost unheard of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-09-2019, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:20:50-07:00","id":931210,"title":"","content":"Still not sure why the Giovanni wants to side with the Sabbat over the Camarilla when the Camarilla has the clear upper-hand; is Augustus disguised or using some sort of Antitribu argument or something to make the Sabbat listen pre-manipulations failure? I also wonder if any Giovanni will (try to) stay in the Cam after most run to the Sabbat out of curiosity.<br /> <br /> On the diablerie bit I wanna confirm: If you're on a Path that advocates Diablerie, you don't lose a Path dot but rather require good roleplay with the whole screwing with the soul thingy lest they be punished with Exp loss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:41:35-07:00","id":931220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931210#post931210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not sure why the Giovanni wants to side with the Sabbat over the Camarilla when the Camarilla has the clear upper-hand; is Augustus disguised or using some sort of Antitribu argument or something to make the Sabbat listen pre-manipulations failure? I also wonder if any Giovanni will (try to) stay in the Cam after most run to the Sabbat out of curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically an attempt to illustrate the difference between the Tremere and the Giovanni. At the end of the day, the Tremere want....Earth to exist. They want the Camarilla, the Masquerade, books, Manchester United, and other things Spike mentions during the Season 2 finale of Buffy. Giovanni...don't. Their ultimate goal is to eventually bring about the end of the world with a necromantic armageddon where the living and dead are one and the Sorcerer God Kings stand at the right hand of their black undead messiah.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni appear human but at the end of the day are as depraved as the Tzimsice.<br /> <br /> Of course, I tend to think of the Giovanni as having the same attitude toward the Endless Night as fundamentalist Christians do to the Biblical apocalypse. Some of them may be SLIGHTLY less enthusiastic about it if they find out that the Day of Judgement isn't some hypothetical day in the future or their grandchildren's future but tomorrow.<br /> <br /> On a more practical note, the Giovanni siding with the Sabbat gives them way more pull than they'd have in the Camarilla. It helps they also know the Antedeluvians are the only people in the world who can actually oppose their plan to destroy the world by opening the Hellmouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the diablerie bit I wanna confirm: If you're on a Path that advocates Diablerie, you don't lose a Path dot but rather require good roleplay with the whole screwing with the soul thingy lest they be punished with Exp loss? </div> </div> </div>To explain one of my Humanity/Path mods, you can regain a lost point of Path with an act of pure expression of the Path or Humanity. I.e. really good roleplaying. You can't RAISE your Humanity or Path this way but you can restore lost dots if that makes sense as a house rule. Path of Caine/Path of Blood followers cannot use Diablerie as this expression because it's fundamentally an act which shakes your sense of self and humanity. You can, however, regain a Point of the Path of Blood by helping another Cainite diablerize someone of lower generation than you or roleplaying your immense devotion to Haquim for a few sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-14-2016, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:43:19-07:00","id":931491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931220#post931220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Giovanni stuff]</div> </div> </div> </div>Righto, I'm with ya.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931220#post931220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain one of my Humanity/Path mods, you can regain a lost point of Path with an act of pure expression of the Path or Humanity. I.e. really good roleplaying. You can't RAISE your Humanity or Path this way but you can restore lost dots if that makes sense as a house rule. Path of Caine/Path of Blood followers cannot use Diablerie as this expression because it's fundamentally an act which shakes your sense of self and humanity. You can, however, regain a Point of the Path of Blood by helping another Cainite diablerize someone of lower generation than you or roleplaying your immense devotion to Haquim for a few sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if your starting Humanity/Path is say 7 then you can regain points up to 7 but not go beyond that without spending Exp?<br /> I think the Path and Diablerie thing is something we're gonna be left disagreeing on so I'll leave it off here. Sufficed to say I do like your house ruling on the above play on regaining Path dots (or else my misunderstanding leading to the conclusion) and have another thing I feel I can use in my games from it; I dare say this was productive overall <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T11:56:58-07:00","id":931497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931491#post931491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righto, I'm with ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if your starting Humanity/Path is say 7 then you can regain points up to 7 but not go beyond that without spending Exp?<br /> I think the Path and Diablerie thing is something we're gonna be left disagreeing on so I'll leave it off here. Sufficed to say I do like your house ruling on the above play on regaining Path dots (or else my misunderstanding leading to the conclusion) and have another thing I feel I can use in my games from it; I dare say this was productive overall <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, that's exactly how it works. It encourages players not to waste experience points but to still pay attention to the Humanity and Path rating. It's basically a lift from Bloodlines where you can gain a point of Humanity from doing something amazingly heroic but personally deterimental or just plain going out of your way to help people for no benefit other than to the right thing. Reuniting E and Lily, helping sire and childe reconcile, or sending Heather Poe away even though she's extremely useful because you want her to have a good life.<br /> <br /> 2. My nerfing diablerie and Paths is basically to encourage diablerie to keep some of its bite. It's something players should be afraid of on one level and reserved for big dramatic moments. One horror story from a friend's game was where the highest generation member of a Sabbat Pack would embrace a bunch of vampires and then proceed to have the other members eat their childer so everyone was within one Generation of the other. That, for me, sucked out all the horror of the thing and turned the act of diablerie into metagaming of the absolute worst sort which they could justify with their Paths. So I wanted to make diablerie a bit more mysterious and dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:14:11-07:00","id":931507,"title":"","content":"<b>Revised Golconda</b><br /> <br /> Golconda is a state where a Kindred is able to mystically join his Beast to his conscious mind and have the two become as one. If a Kindred is not possessed of sufficient willpower to tame the Beast then he is consumed and dies during his Sunspire. The state of Golconda was mentioned in the Book of Nod as being a Gift from God which would allow Kindred to be forgiven but a similar state called The Black Rebirth exists for Path followers which is functionally identical.<br /> <br /> The first recorded Kindred to achieve Golconda was Zao-Lot, the Salubri Antedeluvian who travelled to the Eastern Lands and went on numerous spiritual quests and journeys, studying with both Euthanatos mages and the Kuei-jin. His achievement of Golconda apparently removed the Clan Flaw from his childer and replaced it with their love of Humanity instead. How the Black Rebirth came to be is questionable, though some believe it was achieved by Set, Caine, Malkav, Haquim, or perhaps just Kindred who weren't so famous.<br /> <br /> The effects of Golconda are manifold with success on the Sunspire immediately granting a choice between a Kindred reverting to human or becoming a kind of spiritually enlightened Kindred instead. The benefits of this transformation are not quite as grandiose as some individuals claim and many Kindred have actually achieved it over the centuries. Hundreds, if not thousands, with the majority of the Salubri, sadly, having been since eradicated.<br /> <br /> <b>Requirements</b><br /> <br /> * A Humanity or Path rating of 7 or above.<br /> * A Willpower score of 7 or above.<br /> * The Sunspire ritual to be successfully RPGed.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefits</b><br /> <br /> * Reversion to humanity with all Disciplines remaining as a form of hedge magic or a full awakening as a Mage if mortality is chosen.<br /> * Vampires lose their Generational barriers on raising Disciplines.<br /> * Vampires suffer lethal rather than aggravated damage from sunlight.<br /> * Vampires require one Blood Point per week rather than per day.<br /> * Vampirs no longer suffer Frenzy<br /> * Vampires no longer suffer Rotschreck.<br /> * Malkavian characters lose their derangement but all other clans keep their flaws.<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws</b><br /> <br /> * A Kindred who fails their Sunspire ritual is instantly consumed by wassail and reverts to Humanity 0 or is destroyed outright.<br /> * Golconda and the Black Rebirth require you to keep your Path or Humanity above 5 or you will lose this state and quickly degenerate to wassail afterward.<br /> * Tremere, Followers of Set, and Baali all consider Golconda to be a dangerous heresy which must be destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:24:43-07:00","id":931512,"title":"","content":"In my games, when a Vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again. 1e's corebook sort of implied this, or more accurately, that Golconda was the penultimate step before regaining one's humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T15:28:01-07:00","id":931639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931512#post931512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, when a Vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again. 1e's corebook sort of implied this, or more accurately, that Golconda was the penultimate step before regaining one's humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it almost seems like Vampires who achieve Golconda and remain Vampires should be only a Path thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T15:35:53-07:00","id":931643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931639#post931639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it almost seems like Vampires who achieve Golconda and remain Vampires should be only a Path thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> You know, CTPhipps, I like you. You have a lot of great ideas and even though we don't agree on everything, you are respectful of my ideas and I am respectful of yours. Plus we both love 1e and the Chicago setting, which is always a plus!<br /> <br /> In short, I think you are one cool dude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T16:58:33-07:00","id":931690,"title":"","content":"1. The week of nightmares does not happen at all and Ravnos are still an independent clan<br /> 2. The Kuei Jin exist but in a different form, it is possible for anyone to become a Kuei Jin they do not have to be asian they are in smaller numbers and hated by many supernaturals<br /> 3. The Gangrel are still apart of the Camarilla even with the large numbers that left. You will find more in the wilds than in the city<br /> 3. City Gangrel are not all part of the Sabbat the city Gangrel have been around since the dark ages taking different names in different lands I.E Greek Gangrel, Norman Gangrel, Polish Gangrel. The catch all term is City Gangrel. The non Sabbat variant pride themselves as up standing civilized individuals but they will still attend Moots held by the main body of their clan. There are more City Gangrel in the Camarilla than normal Gangrel<br /> 4. The Tlaique descend from the smoking mirror who may actually not be a vampire but an actual god, I keep this vague because I like the ability to have players form their own opinions on this subject. But they do not descend from Set what so ever and have almost no connection to Caine. The Tlaique get along very well with shape changers, to the point where a tribe of Werejaguars in south America defend the sleeping grounds of Methuselahs and elders.<br /> 5. Werewolf The Forsaken replaces Apocalypse. There is no Wyrm, Gaia, Pentex, Garou, or Umbra. The spirit world has been replaced with the Shadow. Werewolves are still feared for being unpredictable monsters but diplomacy has worked many a time with the Forsaken and Pure tribes. Werewolves keep to themselves mostly working towards their own goals and leaving vampires alone unless it would help them in the long run. Gangrel,Nosferatu, and Tlaique have had the most dealings with the shapechangers.<br /> 6. Hunter the Vigil has been translated over to my setting. The Society of Leopold is more preset than before, Cherion is my Pentex at this point having their hands in the economic pie and offering a supernatural body part black market,<br /> 7. I have changed some rules for Thaumaturgy raising some rituals to top tier because they are overpowered as all hell<br /> 8. Vampire and Werewolf claws only do aggravated damage to humans (mages as well but they do have their spheres to protect them) claws do lethal to supernaturals but of course there is a combination discipline to make claws more potent &quot;Fenrir's Talons&quot; and Werewolves have a Shadow gift to allow Agg on their first attack of a combat.<br /> 9. The Maelstrom did not happen<br /> 10. Kupala is a primordial earth bound that is connected to the Forsaken and Koldonic sorcery directly manipulates the Shadow<br /> 11. Berlin by night did not happen<br /> 12. There are enough Lasombra in the Camarilla to warrant them a Primogen in some cities<br /> 13. Sin-Eaters exist as antagonists to Wraiths<br /> 14. Changling The Lost is Canon in my world<br /> 15. The Tzimisce have a good deal of members within the Camarilla even with the Tremere presence. These fiends are tolerant enough to even be allowed within chantries provided it is necessary<br /> 16. The Dunsirn family descends from cannibalistic Wolf-Bloods of the Ivory Claws<br /> 17. Werewolf Vampire crossbreeds exist in a way with the Dead Wolves bloodline of Gangrel<br /> 18. Baba Yaga is Nosferatu but technically is connected with the Darklings of the Fae<br /> 19. The Sabbat have enforced a rigid cleansing of infernalism in their sect. The Sabbatic Inquisition fight with a horrifying zeal against infernalists destroying entire packs of vampires sabbat or not if they had one member be possibly tainted by the devil<br /> 21. Prometheans do exist within my setting and can be created by anyone with the know how<br /> 22. Vampire The Masquerade Bloodlines is Canon in all my chronicles<br /> 23. There are some Salubri warriors that did not join the sabbat but they are rarely seen outside the middle east<br /> 24. Mages are much less Pulp and much more monstrous in my setting<br /> 25. The Technocracy has less power within the government they still have agents within the government but the Traditions have more as well<br /> 26. The Children Of Osiris do and don't exist, through history they existed but in modern day few remnants of their clan remain. Supernatural and human treasure hunters have come across old temples they built across the world and rumors persist of a sanctum hidden somewhere in the depths of eygpt's sands that holds dozens of vampires and other monsters that where mummified but still alive. <br /> 27. I am in the process of creating more bloodlines for north america and south america, Native American bloodlines that are even more proof that the Caine myth may be wrong.<br /> 28. The Anda survived into the modern nights but are almost unheard of outside asia, currently they are said to be at war with the Lupines of Mongolia The Eaters Of The Dead, rumors speak of an alliance with the Kuei-Jin but no one knows if this is true or not or which side the Kuei-Jin will join.<br /> 29. Colorado is hotly contested over by the Sabbat and Independent Kindred who dwell there. An all out war has been waged through the rocky mountains since 2012<br /> 30. Michigan is divided down the middle with the Sabbat controlling Detroit and the Camarilla controlling Muskegon. Northern Michigan is traversed with caution due to the large amount of Lupines and other strange beasts who stalk the forests and towns. Mackinaw island boasts a strong population of angered shades but the isle is also the site of a great locus known as Sugar Loaf the highest point of Mackinaw. Lupines have made many pilgrimages to this great Locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","user":"The Anubi","date":".  added a few more to the list 07-15-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T01:47:40-07:00","id":931888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931643#post931643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, CTPhipps, I like you. You have a lot of great ideas and even though we don't agree on everything, you are respectful of my ideas and I am respectful of yours. Plus we both love 1e and the Chicago setting, which is always a plus!<br /> <br /> In short, I think you are one cool dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the love.<br /> ...<br /> But ye I agree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Werewolf The Forsaken replaces Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you run with Fera or do you use nWoD Shapechangers to represent Werejaguars? Or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. I have changed some rules for Thaumaturgy raising some rituals to top tier because they are overpowered as all hell</div> </div> </div> </div>What rule changes did you make?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. Vampire and Werewolf claws only do aggravated damage to humans (mages as well but they do have their spheres to protect them) claws do lethal to supernaturals but of course there is a combination discipline to make claws more potent &quot;Fenrir's Talons&quot; and Werewolves have a Shadow gift to allow Agg on their first attack of a combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! What are the Discipline requirements? I believe I'm gonna use this myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. Sin-Eaters exist as antagonists to Wraiths</div> </div> </div> </div>But not as PCs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">15. The Tzimisce have a good deal of members within the Camarilla even with the Tremere presence. These fiends are tolerant enough to even be allowed within chantries provided it is necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are letting Tzimisce (Antitribu) into their chantries? Huh. Or did I misunderstand?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">16. The Dunsirn family descends from cannibalistic Wolf-Bloods of the Ivory Claws</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, gonna consider this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">17. Werewolf Vampire crossbreeds exist in a way with the Dead Wolves bloodline of Gangrel</div> </div> </div> </div>So only Gangrel can embrace Werewolves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">18. Baba Yaga is Nosferatu but technically is connected with the Darklings of the Fae</div> </div> </div> </div>As in she is an embraced Changeling of the Darkling Seeming?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931690#post931690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">22. Vampire The Masquerade Bloodlines is Canon in all my chronicles</div> </div> </div> </div>All of it? Also what about Redemption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T02:56:28-07:00","id":931898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931643#post931643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> You know, CTPhipps, I like you. You have a lot of great ideas and even though we don't agree on everything, you are respectful of my ideas and I am respectful of yours. Plus we both love 1e and the Chicago setting, which is always a plus!<br /> <br /> In short, I think you are one cool dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww, thanks man. Right back at you.<br /> <br /> Love your ideas.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, I actually don't take the whole magical girl thing you describe as all that silly since I occasionally throw in a bit of absolute weirdness to my games which is lighter hearted than the rest of the setting to underscore the World of Darkness COULD be a lot lighter.<br /> <br /> These include Caine (or someone who thinks he is and is powerful enough to make a good case) owning a cab company and refusing to involve himself in vampire affairs.<br /> <br /> A NPC cop friend of the PCs who has the Witchblade which was created by Changelings and struggles to deal with the fact someone actually created a magical artifact in a personal horror game based on a comic book (complete with clothing tearing she hates).<br /> <br /> A similarly powerful ancient human mage mage running a greasy spoon that she runs.<br /> <br /> A Hollow One who is totally not an adult Nico Minrou from The Runaways and goes around the city exorcising ghosts with her staff.<br /> <br /> This is in otherwise a serious melancholy campaign about Kindred mythology and darkness. It's the same attitude when I wrote my &quot;The Rules of Supervillainy&quot; novels as humor helps give some levity between the seriousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T08:28:26-07:00","id":932020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=931888#post931888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you run with Fera or do you use nWoD Shapechangers to represent Werejaguars? Or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> I use NWod shapechangers the Werejaguars are from the Changing Breeds book the Obsidian Shadows who hunt humans mainly.<br /> <br /> What rule changes did you make?<br /> <br /> I make a few rule changes moving rituals like incorporeal passage and Flaming weapon to level 5 because those are very overpowered and should be guarded more by the tremere<br /> <br /> Interesting! What are the Discipline requirements? I believe I'm gonna use this myself.<br /> <br /> Protean 3 and Potence 4 this costs an initial 4 blood to use and it requires you to spend another blood every turn to continue using it. Claws grow in to claws of a primordial beast that even some Lupines say is a sign that vampires are connected to their race<br /> <br /> But not as PCs?<br /> They can but I have not translated all the rules over yet, Sin-Eaters I play up as a mystery to the world. They do work closely with the Giovanni and even the Samedi. Some say even the True Black Hand boasts a few fog bleeding agents.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are letting Tzimisce (Antitribu) into their chantries? Huh. Or did I misunderstand?<br /> <br /> Yes it can happen the antitribu are more inclined to magic and science in my games and to be a part of the antitribu you need to swear an oath to the Camarilla that you will not seek vengeance against clan Tremere or be hunted. Some have proven themselves to the point of where they have been allowed in Chantries but most leave the Tremere to their own devices. Still the modern nights make strange bedfellows<br /> <br /> Interesting, gonna consider this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> So only Gangrel can embrace Werewolves?<br /> <br /> No I should have explained better, Dead Wolves are a refined hybrid created by the Gangrel it is possible for other vampires to embrace Werewolves but those who try mostly create mad empty wolves that have lost a good deal of their spiritual connection. Still playing around the rules for this because the Dead Wolves still have a spiritual connection and act as envoys between the clans and Tribes in the American south. Dead Wolves run on a Humanity Score.<br /> <br /> As in she is an embraced Changeling of the Darkling Seeming?<br /> <br /> It is a mystery but her connection is there, some say she may have been a fae blooded human or Changeling or just has some unearthly connection to the Fae Folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I consider redemption Canon some what<br /> <br /> All of it? Also what about Redemption?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","user":"The Anubi","date":". 07-15-2016, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T19:19:49-07:00","id":932322,"title":"","content":"How Vampires and Other Supernaturals Interact in the &quot;Merged WOD&quot;<br /> <br /> I run a full-on interconnected World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mage: The Ascension</b>: The Technocracy (known as the Illuminati to Vampires) have a treaty with the Camarilla which they cooperate in enforcing the Masquerade. This is the major reason why it's damn near impossible to expose the supernatural. The Tremere are constantly infiltrating and manipulating the Traditions to their own ends with many lower-level mages Embraced. Roughly 80% of the Traditions and Technocracy are Hedge Mages too so vampires are actually pretty top-shelf anyway. Sabbat Cities are often at war with Mages as well with vampire hunters of the Akashic Brotherhood, Celestial Choir, Euthantos, and Technocracy often cooperating. The Kue-jin and Akashic Brotherhood are particularly hateful toward one another. Notably, the Hollow Ones tend to be friendlier with vampires than they are with their fellow mages and many are either ghouled or associates with Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Notably, in my games, the True Hand and have vampires and Euthanatos as equals.<br /> <br /> Note: In my games the destruction of the Ravnos Antedeluvian (actually just Hazimel) was a joint Camarilla/Technocracy action.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b>: Most Camarilla cities have treates between the Lupines and the vampires, which is something that the lesser ranks of the Garou Nation only begrudgingly admit. These treates are designed to enforce the status quo of, &quot;Not my problem.&quot; The Sabbat, of course, have no such treaties and the conflicts with them are much-much worse (are we seeing a pattern here?). Pentex is mostly controlled by vampires now that the Technocracy has eliminated the majority of the Nephandi, Baali, and Wyrm cultists in its upper ranks with the Camarilla using it to increase their power dramatically.<br /> <br /> The relationship between shapechangers and Kuei-Jin are pretty friendly actually as the latter often employ the former as mercenaries and assassins.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Changeling: The Dreaming</b>: The Sabbat is actually quite friendly with the Shadow Court and the most hardcore Unseelie. Parties with the Lasombra or Tzimisce often include members who are judged off-limits. This is basically a reversal of their relationship with every other supernatural and why the Sabbat often have an abundance of magical trinkets which dwarfs the Camarilla's own members. Weirdly, the Sabbat cause the Unseelie to prosper in their territories and they tend to have a 2-3 times the size of normal feelings as the Sabbat's hellraising cause people to believe more in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> House Gwydion, House Scathatch, and House Fiona often have vampire hunting as a rite of passage with most Camarilla Kindred assuming they're just particularly skilled hunters or hedge mages. The Tremere have been known to ghoul or teach House Eiuland kinian with some small overlap between the two. Sluagh also deals with vampires, of all stripes, selling magic or necromancy for blood. Contrary to popular mythology, Malkavians and fairies have very little to do with one another. The Kiyasad are also considered something of a myth by all factions.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b>: Ghosts are the most encountered problem by vampires, even if it's not particularly important in many respects. Ghosts routinely harass vampires as they tend to accumulate victims over the years. This often results in things like burning havens (less so since electrical lights became fashionable), horrible nightmares, visions, and just trashing the places. As such, the Tremere do a thriving business in exorcising havens even if they often have to subcontract the work to mages or Sluagh. The Giovanni have more direct methods of doing so and often develop a thriving trade in boons for it. Anarchs are forced to rely on Hollow Ones and just burning their former havens down.<br /> <br /> Roughly 80% of all vampires become wraiths when they die, higher than any other group except mediums. This is due to the high amount of concentrated deathly energy they have. Vampires tend to form the backbone of the Hierarchy when they don't become specters.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Demon: The Fallen</b>: Demons actually avoid vampires for the most part because every vampire reminds them of Caine and they tend to have a superstition that to harm a vampire is to invoke 7 times the wrath of God, which most vampires would find ridiculous. However, it's not entirely unheard of as bad luck seems to have followed most of those demons who have dealt with them. The Baali, obviously, a brisk relationship with the Infernal but are most interested in either keeping the Earthbound imprisoned or freeing them along with Demon Lords. The Tremere, by contrast, also deal with Demons but use Goetism and very finely worded contracts to keep everything on the level. The Giovanni, similarly, have many deals with the infernal but seem to consider the destruction of reality by them a good thing so they take less precautions. The Tzimsice generally prefer to deal with Banes than true demons even as they often know all of Kupala's demon servitors (Kupala being an Earthbound in this game).<br /> <br /> The Salubri Antitribu, missing the memo the Sabbat's titles are ironic, have devoted themselves to eradicating the demonic infestation on Earth.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Followers of Set HATE demons and have a large number of sorcerers devoted to their banishment or destruction. They call these the Children of Apep and consider it their duty to ward the planet against them.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Hunter: The Reckoning</b>: There are 1,000 Imbued in my world and whenever one dies, another is Imbued. They basically form about 10% of the Hunters in the world even if they're not terribly effective. Vampires are a common enough enemy for them even though they primarily deal with wraiths and zombies and banes. Obviously, their relationship with vampires tends to be on the bad side.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Camarilla has a standing policy of not killing Hunters versus just sending them against the Sabbat or Werewolves or other parties. They generally consider Hunters to be more annoyance than enemy and help keep the vampire population down. The only exception is when they try to break the Masquerade and then the Hammer comes down.<br /> <br /> Have you noticed the Camarilla prefers diplomacy and manipulation to open conflict?<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Kindred of the East, Risen, and Mummies</b>: In general, I tone down the Kuei-Jin &quot;Yellow Peril&quot; elements and highlight they tend to get along with Western Vampires the way any Prince does to people muscling in on their territory, not well but they're willing to get along as long as the niceties are followed.<br /> <br /> There's Western vampires in Kuei-Jin cities and Kuei-Jin in Western cities with no one engaging in any large-scale wars between the two sects. In general, Chinatowns and neighborhoods tend to be territories other Kindred avoid unless they have permission of the local Kuei-Jin. I also make Bloodlines canon with the destruction of the Anarch Free States done by Ming-Xiao working with the Camarilla. However, this was actually due to the fact Ming-Xiao was an Akuma working for the Yama Kings to kill as many racist young Kuei-Jin warriors as possible while also making large numbers of concessions from the Camarilla. It also didn't work in the long run thanks to <b>The Neonate</b>.<br /> <br /> Mummies in my game are a bit more NWoD than OWoD as there's Egyptian mummies, Incan Mummies, Celtic Mummies, Russian mummies, and others working for the Gods of Old. There's also Christian Mummies who the most famous of is <b>Sullivan Dane</b>. They're generally hostile to Kindred but not interested in outright war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2019, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:00:11-07:00","id":932372,"title":"","content":"For me the Camarilla and Technocracy tend to have an unspoken &quot;You leave me alone, I leave you alone&quot; deal going on and listens to whichever presence is the strongest around within reason. Neither wants anymore conflicts with the other than they have to; it's counter-productive.<br /> Werewolves largely do their thing and if they don't fuck with the Kindred then chances are the Kindred are not gonna fuck with them either. That's not always enough to stop either side though.<br /> <br /> As for Demons, the Vampires outnumber the Fallen by far by virtue that most Fallen are still struggling with getting out of the Abyss and are very spread out and limited in number (they cannot pro-create, many are stuck in the Abyss and if one is destroyed outright then they're permanently down in numbers. Otherwise though it's not uncommon for Demons to step on Vampire's toes and vice versa; but they try to stick to their own devices generally speaking. Notably the True Fae have a strange aversion to them and go as far as abandoning prey just to avoid them, the intended (though less &quot;canon&quot;) hint being that there is a connection there; something had to have happened to the Angels who chose neutrality in the war right? Whatever the case, it's not particularly well-known as a phenomenon yet by most people, but it is giving those Lost who notice it either hope, fear or both. Afterall, they can drive away the Keepers through mere presence (if unintentionally), but at the same time, what does that say about the Fallen if even the Gentry is seemingly afraid of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:25:10-07:00","id":932379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=932372#post932372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the Camarilla and Technocracy tend to have an unspoken &quot;You leave me alone, I leave you alone&quot; deal going on and listens to whichever presence is the strongest around within reason. Neither wants anymore conflicts with the other than they have to; it's counter-productive.<br /> Werewolves largely do their thing and if they don't fuck with the Kindred then chances are the Kindred are not gonna fuck with them either. That's not always enough to stop either side though.<br /> <br /> As for Demons, the Vampires outnumber the Fallen by far by virtue that most Fallen are still struggling with getting out of the Abyss and are very spread out and limited in number (they cannot pro-create, many are stuck in the Abyss and if one is destroyed outright then they're permanently down in numbers. Otherwise though it's not uncommon for Demons to step on Vampire's toes and vice versa; but they try to stick to their own devices generally speaking. Notably the True Fae have a strange aversion to them and go as far as abandoning prey just to avoid them, the intended (though less &quot;canon&quot;) hint being that there is a connection there; something had to have happened to the Angels who chose neutrality in the war right? Whatever the case, it's not particularly well-known as a phenomenon yet by most people, but it is giving those Lost who notice it either hope, fear or both. Afterall, they can drive away the Keepers through mere presence (if unintentionally), but at the same time, what does that say about the Fallen if even the Gentry is seemingly afraid of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still debating whether Demons are actual Demons or just Christian themed Fae who are more potent because more people believe in demons than Fae.<br /> <br /> Like the Fae, they believe their own dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:37:39-07:00","id":932386,"title":"","content":"For my part I run with &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; moreso than outright Demon. Worth noting that I also have Infernal Demons from World of Darkness: Inferno around- obviously not the sort who had anything to do with the Abyss -which adds a bit of mystery on where they came from and what, if any, connections they have. Sufficed to say they fill the &quot;always chaotic evil&quot; shoes whereas the Fallen are significantly more individualistic in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T09:17:06-07:00","id":932536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=932386#post932386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my part I run with &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; moreso than outright Demon. Worth noting that I also have Infernal Demons from World of Darkness: Inferno around- obviously not the sort who had anything to do with the Abyss -which adds a bit of mystery on where they came from and what, if any, connections they have. Sufficed to say they fill the &quot;always chaotic evil&quot; shoes whereas the Fallen are significantly more individualistic in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>*scribbles down notes for that*<br /> <br /> We had a hilarious scene in a &quot;cold opening&quot; where the more heroic action-orientated PCs burst in a hilariously stereotypical Satanic ritual (black robes, abandoned church, infant to sacrifice, upside down crosses) where the Ritemaster corrected them that they worshiped the Great Beast, the Wyrm, and weren't demon worshipers.<br /> <br /> Only for one of the cultists to be offended as he thought they were worshiping Satan.<br /> <br /> Another thought they were just being ironic with the murder.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T11:49:08-07:00","id":932582,"title":"","content":"I often change the population composition of the clans to make them more believable from my pov.<br /> <br /> Examples are<br /> <br /> Tremere are dominantly female in the adept circles, complete female chantries or at least 75% are almost the standard.<br /> Lasombra fairly equal, Lasombra Anti strong male majority.<br /> Ventrue mixed, depending on country<br /> Brujah slight female lead<br /> Toreador mixed<br /> Gangrel, slight female lead<br /> Tzimisce depends strongly on country, the more north slavic the more women<br /> Malks strong male lead<br /> <br /> Rest stays similar to the canon<br /> <br /> Gangrel stay in the Cam, week of nightmare happens and is used to show that the Antes are killable and no gods. The Ravnos are not wiped out, they do understand what happend and try to warn Cam vampires, which makes them even less likes. <br /> <br /> When the Demons come to earth they are contacting the Cam first and try to make alliances, the Tremere develop ways to deal with them: either bind them to trinkets or literally get them back to the abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:39:05-07:00","id":932596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=932582#post932582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>Bizarrely, female Tremere are almost completely absent in my game being a relatively recent addition to the Clan but Lasombra are a slight majority of women.<br /> <br /> Malks also make up the majority of the Path of Lilith as the female prophetess is a very common embrace for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T14:27:45-07:00","id":932635,"title":"","content":"The reason for my idea of so many female Tremere is the following:<br /> <br /> Being a Tremere adept is not that great, but the big majority are. If you look at real life examples of corporations you will see that the middle management has a strong female notch. Reasons for that are many, but as many here will agree the Tremere are infact run like a corporation or a very strict order. Therefore it made sense to me to use a gender template that fits that structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T16:57:04-07:00","id":932677,"title":"","content":"I don't see how gender plays into any of this, but okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T17:05:05-07:00","id":932681,"title":"","content":"A semi-canon but fun thing in my games was when the players met Caine at his cab company and had the following conversation:<br /> <br /> * Yes, I'm the first vampire.<br /> * No, I'm actually not the 3rd human being.<br /> * My parents were uplifted humans beloved by a set of gods who had cast them out of their realm.<br /> * No it wasn't the Hebrew God. He was a god at the head of a pantheon, though.<br /> * No, you wouldn't know his name but he was God of the Sun.<br /> * Gods used to be much more common. Now they're not.<br /> * I was cursed to never suffer rest so I arose from the dead after I died. Those who shared my blood were similarly cursed. Sharing blood was loopholing it, I admit.<br /> * Yeah, I suppose it's similar to the Kuei-Jin but it's kind of racist to make everything linked together dontcha think?<br /> * A woman taught me magic, call her Lilith if you want but it's not her actual name. That's how I made my Disciplines.<br /> * Enoch was real but it wasn't called that and it was the same city as the Second City, just rebuilt. There was no Flood.<br /> * It was about 10,000 to 15,000 years ago. This kind of thing gets a bit blurry before calendars.<br /> * The Bible is full of crap. So is the Book of Nod but there's some elements which are true.<br /> * The Creation Myth is from the Followers of Set who taught it to mortals which included the Hyksos who were friendly with the Jews at one point.<br /> * There's no Second Generation, I actually embraced all of the Antedeluvians.<br /> * There were about 52 rather than 13 of them. Quite a few are gone now due to the Jyhad.<br /> * I did, in fact, curse them because they were assholes. I wanted to teach them humility and failed miserably.<br /> * Most of them are dead and they've killed each other a few times actually.<br /> * If you want to call it Cyclical Gehenna, sure.<br /> * The last time I intervened in Kindred Society was when I helped my youngest children overthrow their Elders in the Dark Ages as well as develop their own morality. That was a royal fuck up.<br /> * Who'd believe you if you told anyone I was here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-16-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T18:52:39-07:00","id":932728,"title":"","content":"None of the major &quot;canon&quot; NPC's exist in my games, I'm mainly referring to the ones who became prominent in the Revised metaplot such as Vykos, Theo Bell, Lucita, Anatole, King Albrecht, and the like.<br /> <br /> There are exceptions. Beckett exists, as do the NPC's found in Chicago by Night 1st Edition, Vampire: The Masquerade 1st Edition's corebook (Malcolm, Shelzza, and the Kindred of Gary), Milwaukee by Night, and the cast of Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines (though the Kuei-Jin have been changed to more traditional Cainite Kindred. Ming Xiao is a Tzimisce elder affiliated with the traditional Chinese vampire courts instead of the Sabbat). I'm on the fence about whether or not I should include the NPC's from Montreal by Night as canon or not. I like the book and it pre-dates Revised, but I don't know. I liked the characters, but they aren't as memorable as the NPC's in Chicago.<br /> <br /> Also, since Sailor Moon and the fan-game Senshi: The Merchandising are part of my WoD, that means the Sailor Scouts, Tuxedo Mask, Queen Beryl and her generals, and some of the civilians (such as Naru and Umino) are technically canon NPC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:12:19-07:00","id":932731,"title":"","content":"I like the CONCEPT of Milwaukee by Night. That's it's basically the Kindred's equivalent of the Night's Watch and Wall. You get sent to Milwaukee to do battle with the Wildlings until you die if you royally screw up.<br /> <br /> Under a Blood Red Moon made that kind of underwhelming, though.<br /> <br /> Also, I could never figure out a good enough reason the Garou and Camarilla would both consider said city to be worth fighting over.<br /> <br /> Then again, this is how I do Garou vs. Vampires when their treaties are broken.<br /> <br /> <b>Player: </b>Prince, Prince!<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin:</b> Yes, Neonate?<br /> <br /> <b>Player:</b> Jeffrey just got killed by a werewolf!<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>Such a shame. Please leave.<br /> <br /> <b>Player:</b> But the werewolf is part of a group who said they're going to kill all the Leeches in the city and let me go to warn you.<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>Well, now I have to move my haven since you came right here but ignoring your stupidity, I'll solve this.<br /> <br /> <b>Player: </b>How's that?<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>Traffic cams and Dominating mortals to remembering every detail of their human appearances. From there, we'll have the FBI run facial recognition<br /> software to learn who they are as well as if they've made any purchases. Lupines don't often have credit cards but some of them might have mortal identities we can use against them. They don't run around the city on all fours so we'll have their license plates run as well as see who might be aiding them.<br /> <br /> <b>Player:</b> And then what?<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>And then we make the lives of their families a living hell. Find one, ghoul him or her, then get everything they know. Lupines are mortal so we'll target them when they're sleeping at night by burning down their havens and filling them with silver bullets while they're having lunch or using the lavatory. Lupines need to shit, after all, and that is an appropriate place to shoot them.<br /> <br /> <b>Player: </b>Damn.<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>Alternatively, we'll make use of their stupid animal brains and leave a big file on the desk of a haven we'll let them find. Someone we don't like, such as Anarchs, which will read Project: Werewolf or something and say the vampires in Mexico are planning a disease to kill all werewolves or maybe a magical ritual. Give some satellite photos or addresses of Sabbat havens there.<br /> <br /> <b>Player: </b>Will that work?<br /> <br /> <b>Lodin: </b>Maybe, maybe not. We can also call in the Hunters. Have some of our contacts on the police contact the identified ones in the city and let it slip about these werewolves. Worst case scenario is some of them die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-16-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T04:35:26-07:00","id":932865,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting thought though: can Vampires Embrace and, uh, Ghoul (Can that be used as a verb? The right verb for this situation?) Kinfolk? I know that Embracing a full-on Garou is only going to end in blood and tears, but what about the Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T07:19:01-07:00","id":932892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=932865#post932865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting thought though: can Vampires Embrace and, uh, Ghoul (Can that be used as a verb? The right verb for this situation?) Kinfolk? I know that Embracing a full-on Garou is only going to end in blood and tears, but what about the Kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, nothing stops them from doing either. One of the most gratitutous but effective scenes from UABRM was the mass embrace of a Kinfolk family, including a toddler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T15:57:47-07:00","id":933620,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I do play a <b>Post-Revised</b> (basically the opposite of your world <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>) game and started it before I played V20 and the other 20 games. To expand on what I posted earlier:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Withering Happened</b>: I basically said that 1/3rd of the vampires of the Earth died in 2000 and it wiped out most of the vampires in South America, Russia, India, and other places the players would never go as well as most of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It also meant there were plenty of unclaimed cities in the Americas but vampires clustered together in New York, Saint Louis, and LA for the most part because of fear. The plague eventually stopped for some reason but the consequences still linger with the common beliefs being it was either a vampire disease, punishment from God, or the antedeluvians draining their prey.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I had this happen because it allowed me to dial down the power of the Sabbat and also vampires in general. It also meant that Neonates like the player characters had potentially far stronger ability to project force than in games where they were tripping over Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> It also helps that no one knows how many Ancients survived either. This is part of the reason why the Setites and Assamites are joining the Camarilla as well as why the Sabbat fell apart but is getting back together now that Ur-Shulgi awoke.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Forsaken War</b>: I basically felt the Garou had something of an advantage in the games which needed to be curbed because they were such dangerous violent predators that it'd be interesting to see them warring against EACH other rather than everyone else. As such, I had the Forsaken event happen. The Garou discovered that Father Wolf (hypothetical totem for the whole of the Garou race) was corrupted by the Wyrm and had been for some time.<br /> <br /> One faction of the Garou wanted to cleanse Father Wolf while the other faction wanted to kill him to end the corrosive effect he was having on them. The murder faction killed Father Wolf before a cleansing could happen and in my games, this has actually had a generally positive effect on the Garou overall in terms of attitude but has also weakened them somewhat.<br /> <br /> It's also triggered a war between roughly two equal sides of the Garou which has more or less screwed their attempts to save the world even more than usual. This also has resulted in the Shapechangers coming out of hiding to basically form their own Alliance which is as strong as either of the garou factions.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Traditions and Technocracy are in an uneasy peace</b>: The Avatar Storm happened almost twenty years ago and killed the majority of the Masters or trapped the others across the Gauntlet, turning them into various kinds of spirits. The Pogrom was suspended and the Technocracy focused instead of trying to deal with rebuilding its shattered power base while the Traditions did the same. Amusingly, this resulted in the Technocracy going to war with Pentex and managing to clean it out after almost a decade (and an economic crisis) while the Traditions focused their efforts on more traditional monster hunting.<br /> <br /> As such, this means that 20 years later, the current Masters are actually PCs from the 90s who HATE the Technocracy in an anarchic but now adult sort of way while the majority of newer mages have never been hunted by them so they don't see the big deal. The same is for the Union who have been at peace w/ the Traditions for 20 years and think of them as weird science-hating yokels but not an existential threat to reality.<br /> <br /> There are people who want to wipe the other out but they're extremists on both sides rather than the majority. The M20 Disparate Alliance also exists because the weakening of the Traditions and Union meant the Crafts and Independents could come out of hiding. Essentially, both of them saying, &quot;Finally, Jesus, the 100 years war had nothing on you guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> It opens a lot of non-Ascension War games as a result.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Reckoning is really a status quo now</b>: With a limited number of Hunters (1,000 at any given time), there's always Hunters present in the World of Darkness and they provide a bit of extra-oomph to groups like the Society of Leopold (who tend to classify Catholic Christian psycho Hunters as &quot;Saints&quot; and anyone else as Witches) and smaller Vigils. It makes it hard for the supernatural as a whole but not impossible. In addition, <b>Slashers</b> are what happens when Hunters act consistently evil until they have the equivalent of 0 Humanity and they develop the powers to kill regular humans in ways which seemed designed to send some sort of message. They also become damn near immortal.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Demons exist but aren't really an apocalyptic danger</b>: Demons didn't exactly change the world like they expected since the Hunter Baali joined the True Hand, the Traditions and Technocracy turned their attention back to the world, Hunters sense demons like lighthouses, plus demons turned out to hate each other as much as anyone else. As such, they've never really formed a society and while there's holes in hell, it's more or less a case of many getting summoned, killed, and going back to hell. The smarter demons generally run cults and are more humane than their fellows (albeit that's not saying much). They're also actively working to keep both the Archdemons and Earthbound asleep.<br /> <br /> Because my WoD isn't COMPLETELY HOPELESS, a few of these Cthulhuean entities have also been truly destroyed by both PCs and other heroes which has also made them cautious. The same thing happened with an Antedeluvian (Lasombra) and other ancient evils.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Changeling: The Nightmare exists</b>: The Formorians retuned and by returned, basically have taken over the Dreaming so that it's now a hostile and dangerous place no Changeling actually ever wants to visit. On the plus side, no Formorians actually want to venture into the physical world and just send their servants to kidnap Changelings to be their servants. Yes, that basically means the Formorians are the Gentry from the Lost. They just don't MAKE changelings in this world--at least that anyone knows about it.<br /> <br /> Changelings have, as a small-small-small compensation, benefited from their Arts and magic getting a power up which puts them roughly on par with Vampire Neonates as they can now use Glamour to heal wounds and don't get Banality from just existing--only showing Changeling existence off to regular mortals. Changeling society as a whole is fucked, though, and reduced to smaller courts and alliances than actual kingdoms.<br /> <br /> In short, my Post-Revised world is one where supernaturals have had the shit kicked out of them but are generally not interested in destroying the world so much as surviving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-18-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:42:02-07:00","id":933970,"title":"","content":"One idea that I had was that Cain wasn't so much the first vampire as much as he is the most recent common ancestor of all currently active vampires. There are (sleeping) vampires older than Cain, but not all currently ctive vampires are descended from all of them. Basically between Catiff, bloodlines and a little thing I called the cross-embrace (in which a dhampir born of one clan is embraced by another, thus creating a new clan that combines the traits of both) clans do merge and split off from each other and Cain is just the point where all those first clans converged into the root of the clans known today.<br /> <br /> The so-called &quot;negative generations&quot; aren't believed to still be around by most believers of the theory, but that's what they would say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:34:56-07:00","id":934315,"title":"","content":"I haven't tried it yet, but I'd really like to try reverting to 1E Vampire factions, where the Anarchs are still a major force. Anarchs seem like more fun than Sabbat. Sabbat are just dicks. Maybe I'm just prejudiced because I'm human and Sabbat vampires would eat me on principle.<br /> <br /> One thing's for sure, I no longer try to make all the different groups' canons work together at once. That way lies unending frustration. Whatever splat I'm running is the most important one in that world. Of course that's probably how the games were intended to be run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T01:55:58-07:00","id":935483,"title":"","content":"Something I do: demonic pacts can overcome Ghouldom, minor Bane possession, suppress Magickal effects and other such things. Full-on possession as well as pacts with other demons are out of the question however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:10:23-07:00","id":936137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=933620#post933620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, I do play a <b>Post-Revised</b> (basically the opposite of your world <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>) game and started it before I played V20 and the other 20 games. To expand on what I posted earlier:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Withering Happened</b>: I basically said that 1/3rd of the vampires of the Earth died in 2000 and it wiped out most of the vampires in South America, Russia, India, and other places the players would never go as well as most of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It also meant there were plenty of unclaimed cities in the Americas but vampires clustered together in New York, Saint Louis, and LA for the most part because of fear. The plague eventually stopped for some reason but the consequences still linger with the common beliefs being it was either a vampire disease, punishment from God, or the antedeluvians draining their prey.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I had this happen because it allowed me to dial down the power of the Sabbat and also vampires in general. It also meant that Neonates like the player characters had potentially far stronger ability to project force than in games where they were tripping over Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> It also helps that no one knows how many Ancients survived either. This is part of the reason why the Setites and Assamites are joining the Camarilla as well as why the Sabbat fell apart but is getting back together now that Ur-Shulgi awoke.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Forsaken War</b>: I basically felt the Garou had something of an advantage in the games which needed to be curbed because they were such dangerous violent predators that it'd be interesting to see them warring against EACH other rather than everyone else. As such, I had the Forsaken event happen. The Garou discovered that Father Wolf (hypothetical totem for the whole of the Garou race) was corrupted by the Wyrm and had been for some time.<br /> <br /> One faction of the Garou wanted to cleanse Father Wolf while the other faction wanted to kill him to end the corrosive effect he was having on them. The murder faction killed Father Wolf before a cleansing could happen and in my games, this has actually had a generally positive effect on the Garou overall in terms of attitude but has also weakened them somewhat.<br /> <br /> It's also triggered a war between roughly two equal sides of the Garou which has more or less screwed their attempts to save the world even more than usual. This also has resulted in the Shapechangers coming out of hiding to basically form their own Alliance which is as strong as either of the garou factions.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The Traditions and Technocracy are in an uneasy peace</b>: The Avatar Storm happened almost twenty years ago and killed the majority of the Masters or trapped the others across the Gauntlet, turning them into various kinds of spirits. The Pogrom was suspended and the Technocracy focused instead of trying to deal with rebuilding its shattered power base while the Traditions did the same. Amusingly, this resulted in the Technocracy going to war with Pentex and managing to clean it out after almost a decade (and an economic crisis) while the Traditions focused their efforts on more traditional monster hunting.<br /> <br /> As such, this means that 20 years later, the current Masters are actually PCs from the 90s who HATE the Technocracy in an anarchic but now adult sort of way while the majority of newer mages have never been hunted by them so they don't see the big deal. The same is for the Union who have been at peace w/ the Traditions for 20 years and think of them as weird science-hating yokels but not an existential threat to reality.<br /> <br /> There are people who want to wipe the other out but they're extremists on both sides rather than the majority. The M20 Disparate Alliance also exists because the weakening of the Traditions and Union meant the Crafts and Independents could come out of hiding. Essentially, both of them saying, &quot;Finally, Jesus, the 100 years war had nothing on you guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> It opens a lot of non-Ascension War games as a result.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Reckoning is really a status quo now</b>: With a limited number of Hunters (1,000 at any given time), there's always Hunters present in the World of Darkness and they provide a bit of extra-oomph to groups like the Society of Leopold (who tend to classify Catholic Christian psycho Hunters as &quot;Saints&quot; and anyone else as Witches) and smaller Vigils. It makes it hard for the supernatural as a whole but not impossible. In addition, <b>Slashers</b> are what happens when Hunters act consistently evil until they have the equivalent of 0 Humanity and they develop the powers to kill regular humans in ways which seemed designed to send some sort of message. They also become damn near immortal.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Demons exist but aren't really an apocalyptic danger</b>: Demons didn't exactly change the world like they expected since the Hunter Baali joined the True Hand, the Traditions and Technocracy turned their attention back to the world, Hunters sense demons like lighthouses, plus demons turned out to hate each other as much as anyone else. As such, they've never really formed a society and while there's holes in hell, it's more or less a case of many getting summoned, killed, and going back to hell. The smarter demons generally run cults and are more humane than their fellows (albeit that's not saying much). They're also actively working to keep both the Archdemons and Earthbound asleep.<br /> <br /> Because my WoD isn't COMPLETELY HOPELESS, a few of these Cthulhuean entities have also been truly destroyed by both PCs and other heroes which has also made them cautious. The same thing happened with an Antedeluvian (Lasombra) and other ancient evils.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Changeling: The Nightmare exists</b>: The Formorians retuned and by returned, basically have taken over the Dreaming so that it's now a hostile and dangerous place no Changeling actually ever wants to visit. On the plus side, no Formorians actually want to venture into the physical world and just send their servants to kidnap Changelings to be their servants. Yes, that basically means the Formorians are the Gentry from the Lost. They just don't MAKE changelings in this world--at least that anyone knows about it.<br /> <br /> Changelings have, as a small-small-small compensation, benefited from their Arts and magic getting a power up which puts them roughly on par with Vampire Neonates as they can now use Glamour to heal wounds and don't get Banality from just existing--only showing Changeling existence off to regular mortals. Changeling society as a whole is fucked, though, and reduced to smaller courts and alliances than actual kingdoms.<br /> <br /> In short, my Post-Revised world is one where supernaturals have had the shit kicked out of them but are generally not interested in destroying the world so much as surviving it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually an interesting way of using and advancing the Revised metaplot. I might even be interested in it and use it in one of my games.<br /> <br /> Also, I have considered incorporating Hunter: The Reckoning into my metaplot-free WoD headcanon, but give them an origin not tied to the Sixth Great Maelstrom. Interestingly, I will tie them and the Messengers into Senshi: The Merchandising.<br /> <br /> The Messengers want humanity to stand up against the darkness and take back the night from evils such as the Wyrm, the Sabbat, the Antediluvians, Nephandi, etc. and so they are awakening humans at random. Children, teenagers, and on occasion, very young adults (21 or younger) become Senshi, and older humans (22 and older) become Imbued. Since children and teens are more innocent and idealistic as a rule, there are more Senshi than there are Imbued. However, Imbued tend to have a higher survival rate in their crusade against the forces of darkness than Senshi do as a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:16:02-07:00","id":936205,"title":"","content":"I sometimes wonder, uninitiated as I am, how comparable is Senshi to Princess the Hopeful? They seem to touch a lot on the same concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:29:22-07:00","id":936340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=936205#post936205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sometimes wonder, uninitiated as I am, how comparable is Senshi to Princess the Hopeful? They seem to touch a lot on the same concept.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> \u200bSenshi is more humorous and fanfic-like, being essentially a parody that is also mechanically functional. and has an in-setting explanation for if you want to play it straight serious.<br /> <br /> Princess is more serious and fleshed out.<br /> <br /> In Senshi, you ARE Sailor Moon, Tuxedo Mask, Cardcaptor Sakura, etc., but in Princess you're more of a generic Magical Girl archetype.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:39:44-07:00","id":936348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=936137#post936137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually an interesting way of using and advancing the Revised metaplot. I might even be interested in it and use it in one of my games.<br /> <br /> Also, I have considered incorporating Hunter: The Reckoning into my metaplot-free WoD headcanon, but give them an origin not tied to the Sixth Great Maelstrom. Interestingly, I will tie them and the Messengers into Senshi: The Merchandising.<br /> <br /> The Messengers want humanity to stand up against the darkness and take back the night from evils such as the Wyrm, the Sabbat, the Antediluvians, Nephandi, etc. and so they are awakening humans at random. Children, teenagers, and on occasion, very young adults (21 or younger) become Senshi, and older humans (22 and older) become Imbued. Since children and teens are more innocent and idealistic as a rule, there are more Senshi than there are Imbued. However, Imbued tend to have a higher survival rate in their crusade against the forces of darkness than Senshi do as a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I think a big part of the problem of the Revised Metaplot is they assumed the events were the interesting parts of the story when it was really the aftermath which was intriguing. Giving them time to settle and germinate means there's all sorts of interesting fallout from events which can be pursued.<br /> <br /> 2. That's a dark dark interpretation of Senshi I'm sorry to say. Of course, I often think a Magical Girl is a good concept for a Exorcist, Changeling, or Marauder mage. I've also had Hollow Ones use gothy-versions of Sailor moon stuff as foci.<br /> <br /> 3. My take on the Messengers is I generally keep them mysterious but focus on the fact the Imbuements look like Miracles to outsider and thus may have been with the Kindred and Mages and Werewolves since the very beginning but were mistaken as True Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:56:07-07:00","id":936355,"title":"","content":"I've had a couple of &quot;gods&quot; show up in my game as well it should be noted because sometimes you want to kill or talk to some deities.<br /> <br /> Not often but sometimes.<br /> <br /> Like in Buffy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-24-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T06:51:31-07:00","id":936520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=936348#post936348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. I think a big part of the problem of the Revised Metaplot is they assumed the events were the interesting parts of the story when it was really the aftermath which was intriguing. Giving them time to settle and germinate means there's all sorts of interesting fallout from events which can be pursued.<br /> <br /> 2. That's a dark dark interpretation of Senshi I'm sorry to say. Of course, I often think a Magical Girl is a good concept for a Exorcist, Changeling, or Marauder mage. I've also had Hollow Ones use gothy-versions of Sailor moon stuff as foci.<br /> <br /> 3. My take on the Messengers is I generally keep them mysterious but focus on the fact the Imbuements look like Miracles to outsider and thus may have been with the Kindred and Mages and Werewolves since the very beginning but were mistaken as True Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, it is dark, but it's not the usual way I interpret Senshi, just an optional way of if you wanted to do a darker, more serious take on the matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:14:04-07:00","id":938542,"title":"","content":"If you want to actually have a contemporary Vampire game, anything set after 2000, you have to get rid of the Week of Nightmares. I would suggest changing canon just enough to reflect the real world, so your players can experience terror. The 'I know that it is probably fiction, but there is nothing that is being said that makes me disbelieve the story' feeling, especially when you use recent events in your story. Like the chaos in the Republican Party and the rise of Trump as a presidential nominee is due to the Sabbat attempting to take over the American presidency from the Camarilla (the increased fear and paranoia that the public will experience under a Trump presidency will cause people to turn to authority figures more, allowing the Sabbat to disguise themselves as authority figures more easily so they can enter people's houses and feed without anyone suspecting anything until they find the bodies the next morning, and then 'Islamic terrorists' will be blamed for the atrocity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:27:06-07:00","id":938548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=938542#post938542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to actually have a contemporary Vampire game, anything set after 2000, <b>you have to get rid of the Week of Nightmares.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact no Ravnos have showed up in my games, there haven't been any reprecussions from it in my ten year on and off game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:51:39-07:00","id":938563,"title":"","content":"The entire country of Bangladesh disappearing? The Sixth Malestrum being caused by the deaths of over one hundred million people due to Technocratic spirit bombs? The release of the Denizens of the Dreaming? The cracks in the seals of the Abyss? The appearance of the Red Star? They were all part of the Week of Nightmares, which inevitably concluding with the end of the world. That is why the Week of Nightmares cannot exist if you have a game set after 2000, not unless all of your games are about the end of WoD.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer to have had a mixed group of supernaturals having dealt with the Antideluvians before they became a problem. The animosity of Fera, Kindred, Kuei-jin, Garou, Mages, and Wraiths suspended just long enough to seal the bastards away for ten thousand years, so that they can become the problem of someone else in the distant future, and then everything goes back to normal (except for, perhaps, a few interesting friendships that tone down the violence just a tiny bit between factions). That way, I am able to have my games start in 2015, with a World of Darkness that appears to be nearly identical to our world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T00:05:41-07:00","id":938656,"title":"","content":"Considering that the WoD is intended to depict a darker and more sordid version of our reality, I would argue that Donald Trump ought to be a pretty typical right-wing American politician by the standards of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:14:24-07:00","id":938743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=938656#post938656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the WoD is intended to depict a darker and more sordid version of our reality, I would argue that Donald Trump ought to be a pretty typical right-wing American politician by the standards of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Donald Trump is strictly amateur hour in my WoD. We're talking full-on Grand Theft Auto style personalities in my world. Yesterday, the PCs went out of their way to avoid hurting cops at the water treatment plant who were shooting at them after thwarting a Sabbat attempt to poison the water-supply with a Tzimisce concoction. Sadly, one of the cops was killed by a surviving Sabbat.<br /> <br /> They then overheard the cops talk about how since the perpetrators got away (the Sabbat now ash) that they'd have to frame some Muslims for it or, if there weren't any in the morgue, get some corpses of &quot;ethnic&quot; youth they could say were American Muslims. As for the dead cop? Eh, no one liked her because she was gay.<br /> <br /> And these were just the random cops of my world. Cheap shot to show how rotted their world was? Yes, but it helped highlight humans are the real monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-28-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:11:39-07:00","id":938813,"title":"","content":"Humans are one type of monster in my games, though the majority of really bad humans in my games are Fomori or are Infernalists. The smart ones who are bad, the majority of the upper classes in each country, are Infernalists. The dumb ones who are bad are Fomori, though some of the Fomori are just unlucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:00:42-07:00","id":938997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=938813#post938813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are one type of monster in my games, though the majority of really bad humans in my games are Fomori or are Infernalists. The smart ones who are bad, the majority of the upper classes in each country, are Infernalists. The dumb ones who are bad are Fomori, though some of the Fomori are just unlucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I try to make regular humans pretty common as evildoers. Pentex, for example, was never more destructive and more dangerous to the WOD than when it was run by human psychopaths unaware of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> It's currently under the Camarilla's control in my games and every bit as dangerous.<br /> <br /> You raise a good point about the Week of Nightmares and I'm going to dramatically scale back the event in my canon. &quot;Only&quot; 100,000 people died in my version and was blamed by a freak combination of a hurricane and earthquake. Conspiracy theorists claim terrorists detonated a stolen nuclear explosive and its a source of pilgrims as well as a major humanitarian disaster area but it's not the ridiculous craziness of the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:03:47-07:00","id":939727,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the death toll from Time of Thin Blood was a lot smaller than 100 million, by a couple of orders of magnitude. Everything was being covered up as the results of particularly catastrophic monsoon flooding, not a major asteroid impact in South Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:56:48-07:00","id":941165,"title":"","content":"In my V:tM games, I usualy don't change up thing, except a few tweaks, but my actual M:tA game, I've fondamentaly changed the supernatural world : There is only Mage and spirits. Vampire, Werewolf, Mummies, they all exist, but a the result of magic. I've recuperated a few element from the other games, and integrated into the Tradition or the Technocracy : for exemple, the Tremere turned themselves into vampire through a a spell that was a corruption of the original Spell of Life, so I could keep the history between them and the Order into the game ;the Fiana are a family part of the Bardic College of the Verbena, the Get of Fenris are anthor name for the Aghalaz of the Cult of Ectasy, the whole Drone concept is an experiment from the Cult of the Machine of Iteration X. <br /> The players, all WOD veterans, like those twist for the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:45:35-07:00","id":941383,"title":"","content":"No crossover in my games; the Lupines that prowl the wilderness and terrify city-dwelling Kindred are minstrous wolfmen, but they aren't organized into Tribes and never talk about any Weaver or Wyrm if we're playing a Vampire chronicle. Likewise, the Technocracy may be aware of nocturnal blood-drinking reality deviants, but those creatures don't claime to be heirs of Caine or fight in a grand Jyhad. Whatever game we're playing is the only one that exists.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, I treat the Baali as a legitimate clan, with the Setites being a significant and populous bloodline among them.<br /> <br /> The Ascension War is a political one far more than an outright pogrom in the streets, largely due to the effects of the Avatar Storm. Am I the only one that vastly prefers Mage Revised to earlier editions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-01-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T15:53:46-07:00","id":941463,"title":"","content":"No Week of Nightmares in my games means no mass escape of Demons. While Demons exist, they are very rare, and only exist when summoned by sorcerers or mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:04:58-07:00","id":941471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=941463#post941463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Week of Nightmares in my games means no mass escape of Demons. While Demons exist, they are very rare, and only exist when summoned by sorcerers or mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Albeit, I generally reverse it so more humane Demons have always been a result of what happens when a demon joins with a human being permanently via possession. Most remain assholes but not ALL of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:45:25-07:00","id":944125,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire:</b> The Week of Nightmares happened alright, and the Red Star is still up there, and if another antediluvian rises a century from now, those guys will really be picking up the the pace compared to the last millennium. How come aeons turn so much slower than new iPhones come out?<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, as a whole, are hypocrites, in that they love humans in principal but aren\u2019t social animals themselves. Their aversion to killing just means they like to keep blood dolls trapped in hellish abusive relationships for decades on end. Their strict laws about individual territory prevents them from socializing much outside of Elysium, and this encourages them to idealize one another. On the whole, each individual in the Camarilla thinks he or she is the only one who\u2019s a horrible person.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> The garou religion is a more accurate interpretation of umbral politics than most other religions, but it\u2019s still a religion. There are mages in the upper echelons of every major world religion who are in contact with ancient spirits, but that doesn't mean they know everything, either. Most spirits have poor memories and narrow ranges of experience, and like telling fleshies what they want to hear.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is a cohesive political faction in the spirit world, but it only originated shortly before the fall of the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> \u201cWeaver spirits\u201d are just spirits that have allied themselves with humanity, and don\u2019t otherwise have a common leadership or necessarily like each other. They typically dislike shapeshifters because shapeshifters are typically dangerous to humans. Some spirits do believe in the Weaver as an ideal, but the universe only cares what humans believe.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Wyld\u201d is wishful thinking that all the spirits who aren't hostile to shapeshifters on general principle have something else in common as well. Many \u201cWyld spirits\u201d have learned to take it as a compliment, some haven\u2019t.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s fair to say the Black Spiral Dancers are bad as werewolves go, but from a human perspective, even the Children of Gaia and Stargazers are in the same moral neighborhood as human organized crime families and terrorist groups.<br /> <br /> Until a little over a century ago, the Black Spirals were almost universally maniacal, hedonistic, rampaging monsters. That was also about when they stopped being one of the smallest tribes.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s now the elder Black Spirals who constitute most of the stereotypical genocidal psychopaths, but those guys aren't happy with most of tribe. While it\u2019s true that the BSDs have major endemic problems with drugs and rape culture, at least half the other tribes can compete in at least one of those departments each.<br /> <br /> The majority of BSDs join because either they\u2019re metis, their kids are metis, or they just don't want to base their lives around garou dogma anymore. Come on, free range beef is expensive. You go to one ritual, and then you lay low and lend crash space to rampaging tweakers when need be so they\u2019ll protect you when your old pack tries to deprogram you with a klaive.<br /> <br /> So the BSDs get the revised Sabbat treatment. It\u2019s not that they\u2019re right, or that they\u2019re nicer folks on the whole than the other tribes, it\u2019s that the problem is the Garou Nation\u2019s bigotry. In themselves, the BSDs are pretty ineffective no matter how you slice it. Their main purposes from the Wyrm\u2019s perspective are to keep werewolves \u201con the bench\u201d and distract the other tribes from real problems.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> The Ascension War is over. At least the first one. Both factions are thoroughly infiltrated by nephandi and/or harbor a lot of widderslaintes who don\u2019t know or care that they\u2019re nephandi. No one\u2019s sure which. Some mages have also been spontaneously going Barrabus since the Avatar Storm started.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy and Traditions are both rapidly splintering. The Celestial Chorus has partially joined the Technocracy. The Void Engineers look like they might go the other way. The Adepts and Euthanatos have more or less gone rogue. The Order of Hermes just doesn\u2019t get much love since the whole Ksifari fiasco, so the Hollow Ones have become the de facto leader Tradition even though they probably harbor the most nephandi. The Iteration X\u2019ers are still fanatically loyal to the Technocracy, if only because of their increasingly vocal adoration of the machine god Autochthon, which really creeps out the rest of the conventions. The Ahl-I-Batin are attempting to rejoin the Traditions, but they\u2019re not sure who\u2019s supposed to ratify that at this point.<br /> <br /> There are also three emerging cross-paradigm group of mages from all the Traditions and the Conventions. The first one is allied with certain demons and imbued, and they don\u2019t have much in common except hatred of (most) non-humans. The second is trying to create a coalition of non-humans. The third faction just doesn\u2019t understand why trafficking with demons is acceptable all of a sudden, and think demons are causing the increase in nephandi.<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith:</b> Demons helped with the relief effort during the Sixth Maelstrom, and have since been rebuilding the Dark Kingdoms in their image. They\u2019ve also created a new type of undead to serve as Stygia\u2019s agents in the land of the living.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling:</b> The Shadow Court has shed its secrecy since the Second Resurgence. The general consensus is that the balance of power between the courts should be restored, but no one is sure how. The general mindset that humans are the enemy is getting more socially acceptable in Concordia, as is modern technology.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> By 2006, the imbued had started organizing into largish cells, and every supernatural faction wanted as many of those cells in its pockets as would fit. By now, most of the imbued are allied with demons and mages and many are trying to convince themselves they\u2019re not mercenaries.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon:</b> Demons are also losing interest in their own factions in favor of throwing in with established players. They\u2019re floaters who don\u2019t have much of a cause of their own since they still can\u2019t find Lucifer. They\u2019re basically seen as the spirit equivalent of an out of work veteran who isn\u2019t allowed near schools driving a car with no plates, so they take what comes their way. A lot of them work for mages and a few have assimilated into changeling society, since they can enter the Dreaming, unlike the Umbra (Heaven).<br /> <br /> I generally use Demon as chassis for my WoD. Fera and vampires are surviving Rabisu and Halaku nephilim, respectively. Vampires, the Underworld, and the Dreaming were all created by demons as attempts to preserve human knowledge across generations. The Umbra is the ruins of Heaven. Spirits are angels, but most of them have lost their consciousness and/or sanity since God was assassinated. The Wyrm is a faction of angels and demons who believe God\u2019s Creation doesn't deserve to exist without God.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and the first generation of nephilim are now in their teens, as is the Pure Metis. This may be bad, because some demons remember something about the original nephilim having been destroyed because when they bred together, their children were more powerful than either parent, so in enough generations they could have rivaled God. Metis infertility was probably why the fera were spared. This process already seems to be setting in with dhampir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:17:14-07:00","id":944422,"title":"","content":"I love this thread I do and am going to throw some just random stuff in about characters and the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortal Authorities</b><br /> <br /> + For a short description of the police in my games, I go with, &quot;Slightly more incompetent and corrupt than the ones in Gotham City.&quot; If the police arrive at a situation involving the supernatural they're likely to cut and run but if they do stay, then they're likely to random shoot at everything and make up whatever story they can.<br /> <br /> The police are almost always under the control of vampires in the WoD but they're unaware of the truth--instead believing they're taking bribes from the uber-rich and mafia of the city. In my WOD, every police station has a room for working over suspects, isolating criminals until they confess to whatever is done, and evidence lockers where cash as well as drugs routinely disappear. It's not at all how I feel about the police in RL save perhaps the worst places in America but it fits my view of the WoD.<br /> <br /> + The United States government and most governments in general have a large amount of knowledge about how the supernatural works. However, virtually all of the people who know are corrupt or working hand-in-hand with them. Generally, when someone finds out the truth, they get visited by the Technocracy or vampires to get offered to be brought into the fold and it works well.<br /> <br /> + Bob Schnoblin was Director of the CIA under George W. Bush.<br /> <br /> + Two Presidents were ghouls and Marcus Vitel used to direct the Federal government by fixing US elections.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b><br /> <br /> + Endron Oil is a stand-in for Enron Oil in my game and went bankrupt in much the same way. However, this being the WOD, it got bailed out by the government and is back to 100% effectiveness.<br /> <br /> Well, it would be except for the fact it's now under vampire management.<br /> <br /> + Harold Zettler is an atheist who doesn't believe in the Wyrm and assumes all of his cohorts are worshiping the Antediluvians or demons while he milks the Pentex cow for all its worth.<br /> <br /> + King Albretch fully believes he's going to be assassinated long before the Apocalypse (and doesn't actually believe in it) but is trying to push whatever reforms he can before it happens.<br /> <br /> + Evan has to hang around Albretch because a Caucasian Wendigo born in the Suburbs is someone no one takes seriously. He's all-but-decided to defect to the Children of Gaia as soon as he can.<br /> <br /> + Albretch and Mari broke the Litany and both are pretty terrified about that being found out (and doing it again).<br /> <br /> + Samual Haight was actually an entirely serious werewolf hunter who killed 20 Garou while mortal before getting his ritual that allowed him to become a Skinwalker. When he died, he was resurrected as an Abomination by his followers before being finally put down. It's only Garou &quot;fireside&quot; and the Nuwisha stories which made him ridiculous.<br /> <br /> + Number Two in Malpheas is the Silver Fang King who began the War of Rage. A lot of the Garou's beliefs about their religion, customs, and practices come from him. The Mokole know this but trying to share that memory usually results in a fight.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b><br /> <br /> + Lucita starred in a bunch of Spanish language exploitation films in the 1970s as she doesn't have a problem with nudity and thought they were awesome. She also starred in a few English ones directed by the Kindred Johann. How she appeared in film is anyone's guess.<br /> <br /> This includes an adaptation of Vampirella.<br /> <br /> + Most Malkavians aren't actually wacky at all but plenty of them play up the stereotype so people will keep them out of the Jyhad. If a Malkavian is doing that, he wants you to leave him the **** alone.<br /> <br /> + Anatole is a master of this despite the fact God and the Antediluvians literally speak to him.<br /> <br /> + Lodin isn't dead is actually a conspiracy theory and Edward Neally eventually had himself Vicissituded to look like his former boss.<br /> <br /> + Balthazar is an enormous Dukes of Hazard fan and the fact he's Canadian with no Southern blood whatsoever is a joke. He's also actually possessed of a staggering resemblance to Charlie Sheen and is quite handsome if he ever bothers to clean up.<br /> <br /> + Beckett is actually a black Londoner (this may be canon).<br /> <br /> + Vykos is a Loyalist in my game and absolutely despises the idea of Sabbat becoming like the Camarilla so he constantly stirrs shit with the younglings and undermines his fellow Elders.<br /> <br /> + Theo Bell is ripping off Wesley Snipe's blade and pretending he came up with it first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-05-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:19:26-07:00","id":944423,"title":"","content":"Awesome write-up, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5553\" data-vbnamecard=\"5553\">Mr. Sluagh</a>. I don't agree with everything but think its still very awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:08:14-07:00","id":949796,"title":"","content":"My vampire games usually borrow from both VtR and VtM. Covenants are sects and they tend to be more aggressive with each other than in the VtR standard setting. <br /> One of the key differences though, is that no vampire knows the true origin of vampirism. There's something like the fog of eternity that messes with the elder's memory. <br /> Vampires in game use the term &quot;bloodline&quot; to refer to clans and Clan is an IC term that refers to those bloodlines that have a standing in the Camarilla and a sit in the Inner Circle. Clans within a city may offer protection to other bloodlines under their Clan banner.<br /> <br /> During character creation players can choose between roughly 35 available different bloodlines (there's like other 10 more that are NPC only) grouped by the VtR categories (Lord, Haunt, Shadow, Beast or Succubi) including the 13 original clans and the 5 VtR standard clans and some of the bloodlines found in the nwod books (some have been homebrewed other merged for example Lygos and Badacelli belong to the same bloodline of blind darkness worshiping underground vampires).<br /> <br /> Werewolves are Lupines instead of the de facto werewolf games. They're divided in three bigger factions: The Pure, The Forsaken and the The Reformed (working on the name). The larger faction are the Reformed which are werewolves trying to coupe with being &quot;cursed&quot; with The Change and try to hold to their own Humanity the most. They chain themselves during the full moon and many try to find cures or rescue other kinfolk or werewolves from the other factions or try to fight back against outsiders a lot like guerrilla style resistant groups. These are the most numerous. Then there's The Pure. Not much is changed except that the Fire Touched are more like a Tribe of darwinian gangs/fanatical group fighting each other for territory. The Forsaken do their thing mostly outside of the cities. Children of Gaia are trying to protect the earth but they're pacifists and healers. Here you can find sone other Fera but for the most part the Childeen are considered legends or folk tales.<br /> (Sorry for my bad English)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12201-brainstr\u00f6m","name":"Brainstr\u00f6m","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T03:55:30-07:00","id":949967,"title":"","content":"How do I modify my WoD setting from the baseline? Gawd, it might be easier (though less fun) to list what I <b>haven't</b> modified. To start with, all the myths and legends of how XYZ came to exist? All myths, all legends. But all have an element of the truth. I created my own Grand Unified Theory (of the World of Darkness) to explain how Garou cosmology fits in with Vampire's Judeo-Christian base. For now, I'll focus on my changes to the big one; Vampire. Some details are left out, since one of my players in-frequents this board and somehow will probably stumble on to this very post and read things I'm not ready to unveil.<br /> <br /> Caine is still the progenitor of his species. He still made the 2nd generation (the &quot;Lost Generation&quot;, according to my notes). The thirteen clans are descended from the Antideluvians, who are all of the 3rd Generation. And Caine is probably the first vampire.<br /> <br /> But not all vampires descend from Caine. I re-tooled the Keui-jin to use the same system as Cainites, then created other &quot;Vampire Variants&quot;. Each of these separate lines of Vampires have different weaknesses and strengths, each come from different areas of the world (some regions even having two or three different &quot;vampire strains&quot;), and each claims their &quot;Patient Zero&quot; was the first vampire. But the Cainite &quot;strain&quot; is the easiest to &quot;pass on&quot;, hence why they're the most wide-spread. Some of these lineages might only have a handful of remaining &quot;carriers&quot;, with the rest having been wiped out in their own, personal apocalypse. Others might have hundreds or thousands of members who coexist among Cainites (including one of the official bloodlines whose origins I retconned). But most are few in number, keep to their &quot;ancestral lands&quot;, and stay out of the spotlight for reasons of their own.<br /> <br /> As for the Cainite Antediluvians, I upped their numbers to (redacted). The thirteen big ones are the most prolific, to be sure. Of the ones remaining, some never sired more than one or two childer (or none at all). Some died during some minor apocalypse or another. A couple formed small clans centered on a specific region. Some had weaknesses so crippling that they and their clans withered away to nothing by the modern nights. But even though there's more than thirteen, only the big thirteen can claim any relevance in the modern nights. Like the other &quot;Vampire Offshoots&quot; (except the K-Js, who have significant enough numbers), these &quot;lesser Antediluvians&quot; are more of a curiosity, a relic of the past, something for a Malkavian scientist obsessed with the origin of the species to research about and include in the footnotes of his papers.<br /> <br /> For the small number of kindred who know about this &quot;broader vampire world&quot;, it brings up new questions about Gehenna. If it's about the Antes rising up and eating all other vampires, does that just mean Cainites, or do the other &quot;strains&quot; suffer at their fangs as well? Or do their own &quot;great-great-grandpappies&quot; rise and eat them while the Antes are chowing down on the Cainites? Are those other guys spared? And when Caine rises up, is he alone? Is his big final confrontation with god, or is it really with these other &quot;lineage progenitors&quot;? And of course, there's always the question about whether the progenitors of these other vampire lineages are actually stories about Caine corrupted by time (or of course, is Caine actually a corruption of their story)? Is the reason some of these lineages are so small and numerically depleted because they already went through their own &quot;Gehenna&quot; and, if so, does that mean Gehenna is something Cainites can survive through, albeit in limited numbers?<br /> <br /> I like to add things like these &quot;Kindred offshoots&quot; whenever it can add some level of doubt to the existing story. Especially when I give the caveat of &quot;all of this, of course, might be clever Setite lies and Malkavian ramblings&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:40:58-07:00","id":955246,"title":"","content":"It's next to impactless in the game, but Avalon Incorporated, the Pentex subsidiary, employs something called the Avalon Standard Dimensions on its action figures. This means that all action figures across all its lines are of the same rough size, meaning that all weapons, vehicles and accessories can be used by all action figures.<br /> <br /> Why? Because with all action figures being compatible they are more fun when playing with many of them at the same time. Which means that kids will want more of them, which in turn is profit for Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:34:08-07:00","id":955277,"title":"","content":"And contamination because each action figure contains a small portion of a bane who presence encourages aggression, racism, and sexism (why else would the vast majority of the action figures be white men?). While only a small portion of the children become possessed, the ones who acquire the complete collection, the profit from the action figures and the suffering caused by the contamination only further the goals if the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:39:21-07:00","id":955320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922283-how-do-you-modify-your-classic-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=955277#post955277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And contamination because each action figure contains a small portion of a bane who presence encourages aggression, racism, and sexism (why else would the vast majority of the action figures be white men?). While only a small portion of the children become possessed, the ones who acquire the complete collection, the profit from the action figures and the suffering caused by the contamination only further the goals if the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Anybody want a balloon?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're not doing that anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay... guess I'll just... float on out of here...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Seriously, banes in products in a thing of the past. It's gone from practical Wyrm talens for sale to things that attract or agitate them to simple, sleazy tactics that bring out normal bad emotions in people as time has moved on. That's the Pentex we're dealing with now - lean, mostly unknown, and disturbingly innocuous.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:44:41-07:00","id":958392,"title":"","content":"Made some edits and editions<br /> <br /> 1. The week of nightmares does not happen at all and Ravnos are still an independent clan<br /> 2. The Kuei Jin exist but in a different form, it is possible for anyone to become a Kuei Jin they do not have to be asian they are in smaller numbers and hated by many supernaturals<br /> 3. The Gangrel are still apart of the Camarilla even with the large numbers that left. You will find more in the wilds than in the city<br /> 3. City Gangrel are not all part of the Sabbat the city Gangrel have been around since the dark ages taking different names in different lands I.E Greek Gangrel, Norman Gangrel, Polish Gangrel. The catch all term is City Gangrel. The non Sabbat variant pride themselves as up standing civilized individuals but they will still attend Moots held by the main body of their clan. There are more City Gangrel in the Camarilla than normal Gangrel<br /> 4. The Tlaique descend from the smoking mirror who may actually not be a vampire but an actual god, I keep this vague because I like the ability to have players form their own opinions on this subject. But they do not descend from Set what so ever and have almost no connection to Caine. The Tlaique get along very well with shape changers, to the point where a tribe of Werejaguars in south America defend the sleeping grounds of Methuselahs and elders.<br /> 5. Werewolf The Forsaken replaces Apocalypse. There is no Wyrm, Gaia, Pentex, Garou, or Umbra. The spirit world has been replaced with the Shadow. Werewolves are still feared for being unpredictable monsters but diplomacy has worked many a time with the Forsaken and Pure tribes. Werewolves keep to themselves mostly working towards their own goals and leaving vampires alone unless it would help them in the long run. Gangrel,Nosferatu, and Tlaique have had the most dealings with the shapechangers.<br /> 6. Hunter the Vigil has been translated over to my setting. The Society of Leopold is more preset than before, Cherion is my Pentex at this point having their hands in the economic pie and offering a supernatural body part black market,<br /> 7. I have changed some rules for Thaumaturgy raising some rituals to top tier because they are overpowered as all hell (I.E Flaming Weapon, The one that lets you phase through objects, Etc.)<br /> 8. Vampire and Werewolf claws only do aggravated damage to humans (mages as well but they do have their spheres to protect them) claws do lethal to supernaturals but of course there is a combination discipline to make claws more potent &quot;Fenrir's Talons&quot; and Werewolves have a Shadow gift to allow Agg on their first attack of a combat.<br /> 9. The Maelstrom did not happen<br /> 10. Kupala is a primordial earth bound that is connected to the Forsaken and Koldonic sorcery directly manipulates the Shadow<br /> 11. Berlin by night did not happen<br /> 12. There are enough Lasombra in the Camarilla to warrant them a Primogen in some cities<br /> 13. Sin-Eaters exist as antagonists to Wraiths<br /> 14. Changling The Lost is Canon in my world<br /> 15. The Tzimisce have a good deal of members within the Camarilla even with the Tremere presence. These fiends are tolerant enough to even be allowed within chantries provided it is necessary for a Tremere to speak with one of the fiends on their own grounds.<br /> 16. The Dunsirn family descends from cannibalistic Wolf-Bloods of the Ivory Claws<br /> 17. Werewolf Vampire crossbreeds exist in a way with the Dead Wolves bloodline of Gangrel and the Danislavs<br /> 18. Baba Yaga is Nosferatu but technically is connected with the Darklings of the Fae<br /> 19. The Sabbat have enforced a rigid cleansing of infernalism in their sect. The Sabbatic Inquisition fight with a horrifying zeal against infernalists destroying entire packs of vampires sabbat or not if they had one member be possibly tainted by the devil<br /> 21. Prometheans do exist within my setting and can be created by anyone with the know how<br /> 22. Vampire The Masquerade Bloodlines is Canon in all my chronicles<br /> 23. There are some Salubri warriors that did not join the sabbat but they are rarely seen outside the middle east<br /> 24. Mages are much less Pulp and much more monstrous in my setting<br /> 25. The Technocracy has less power within the government they still have agents within the government but the Traditions have more as well.<br /> 26. The Children Of Osiris do and don't exist, through history they existed but in modern day few remnants of their clan remain. Supernatural and human treasure hunters have come across old temples they built across the world and rumors persist of a sanctum hidden somewhere in the depths of eygpt's sands that holds dozens of vampires and other monsters that where mummified but still alive.<br /> 27. I am in the process of creating more bloodlines for north america and south america, Native American bloodlines that are even more proof that the Caine myth may be wrong.<br /> 28. The Anda survived into the modern nights but are almost unheard of outside asia, currently they are said to be at war with the Lupines of Mongolia The Eaters Of The Dead, rumors speak of an alliance with the Kuei-Jin but no one knows if this is true or not or which side the Kuei-Jin will join.<br /> 29. Colorado is hotly contested over by the Sabbat and Independent Kindred who dwell there. An all out war has been waged through the rocky mountains since 2012<br /> 30. Michigan is divided down the middle with the Sabbat controlling Detroit and the Camarilla controlling Muskegon. Northern Michigan is traversed with caution due to the large amount of Lupines and other strange beasts who stalk the forests and towns. Mackinaw island boasts a strong population of angered shades but the isle is also the site of a great locus known as Sugar Loaf the highest point of Mackinaw. Lupines have made many pilgrimages to this great Locus.<br /> 31. The Einherjar where not in fact wiped out in the Fenrir wars, in my setting the Blood Talons got a long quite well with the Afterganger but the coming of the White Christ brought destruction to the Einherjar there are those who survived into the modern age such as Odin but he was<br /> 32. The Danislav Revenant family survived into the modern era by means of their distant family within the Storm Lords Tribe who saved them after the death of the Fiend who created the Danislav line. They are used primarily by the Lodge Of Crows but as a gesture of diplomacy they where also allowed to work within the Ordea League so the Lodge could create an alliance with the Old Kings. They also have the ability to use Shadow Gifts of the Storm Lords<br /> 33. The Giovanni did not kill all of the Cappadocians there are several who survived into the modern era and are considered a bloodline as of current and are hunted by the Giovanni when they are able to.<br /> 34. New Orleans by night is not Canon, and the Grand Masquerade thing is somewhat canon. Been toying with the idea that it is Camarilla exclusive plus a few independent clans but there is a very specific amount of vampires allowed at any given Grand Masquerade, and if they want to bring guests of Kindred or Non-Kindred persuasion they have to discuss it with the planners of the event.<br /> 35. The Samedi do have their own forms of Necromantic rituals and a path I am creating for them based off of Voodoo. Such as a ritual that creates a rum that is infused with the blood of a man who pleaded guilty to a crime he committed which allows the imbiber of the rum to be harassed by the spirits of those who they murdered or harmed in life which lasts for an entire day and night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}